NCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Tax Foreclosure Division**\n**Case:** TX-23-00042 | **Court:** 160th District Court (Judge Carl Ginsberg)\n**Subject Property:** Dallas, TX 75215 (38th/Atlanta St corridor) | **Classification:** CRITICAL — Priority Pursuit\n**Prepared By:** Senior Acquisition Analyst | **Date:** June 2025\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is overwhelmingly a **land play, not a structure play.** The DCAD data tells the full story: a 558-square-foot structure built in **1936** carrying **60% depreciation** sits on this lot, placing the physical improvement at or near the end of its economic life. At 89–90 years old, the structure has almost certainly exhausted its useful life for any conventional financing or resale to a retail buyer without gut rehabilitation — and given the 558 sq ft footprint, rehabilitation economics are deeply questionable at nearly any cost basis. The critical ratio here is the **land-to-improvement split**: with a $72,740 DCAD market value and a structure this depreciated, the land underneath is carrying the bulk of that assessed number. Dallas County''s 75215 zip code (South Dallas/Atlanta Street corridor) has been an active infill and assemblage target, which means the dirt itself has real speculative and development value independent of anything sitting on it. Demolition and a cleared lot, or a hold-and-assemble play, is the exit thesis — not a renovation flip.\n\nThe ownership picture is **fragmented and legally complex.** DCAD shows title vested 100% in **"Motley, Mrs. James A"** — almost certainly **Cora Pearl Motley**, who appears as a defendant in this case with address listed as unknown and **unserved** as of the docket. The deed transfer date of **1/1/1900** is a DCAD placeholder indicating no recorded transfer in the modern instrument record — meaning this property has likely passed through informal succession, verbal inheritance, or simply sat untransferred for decades. The last tax payment on record under the Motley name was **2014** — eleven years of zero payments. Before Motley, **Gerre G. Williams** paid taxes through approximately **1993**, suggesting the Williams family held this property and either conveyed it to Cora Pearl Motley (possibly a family member or heir) or allowed title to drift. The defendant list — Ruby J. Williams (served by posting, address unknown), Gerre Ganell Williams (3926 Atlanta St, Dallas 75215), Willie A. Williams,','\n',char(10)),'More complex than TX-26-00009 (Rogers) due to estate situation with 10 defendants vs 1, and heir complications requiring attorney ad litem appointment.','judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-12T14:33:24.445325','2026-07-09 05:04:50','2026-07-08T19:13:18.083952',1,'individual','high','Being Lot Number Seven (7) of Block ''B'' of Oak Grove Addition, an addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded in Volume 2537 Page 125 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','{"account_number": "00000172327000000", "market_value": 72740, "land_value": 34820, "improvement_value": 37920, "estimated_annual_taxes": 1619.71, "year_built": 1936, "effective_year_built": 1936, "actual_age": 90, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "POST", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 558, "total_area_sqft": 558, "bedrooms": 0, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 60, "desirability": "FAIR", "air_condition": "WINDOW", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "PLANNED DEVELOPMENT DISTRICT", "lot_frontage_ft": 32, "lot_depth_ft": 91, "lot_area_sqft": 3482.0, "land_unit_price": 10.0, "legal_description": "1: OAK GROVE 2: BLK B/1729 LT 7 3: 4: 5: 1729B000 007 1001729B000 Deed Transfer Date: 1/1/1900", "owners": [{"name": "MOTLEY MRS JAMES A", "pct": 100}], "deed_transfer_date": "1/1/1900", "exemptions": "None", "no_homestead": true, "tax_rates": [], "current_tax_balance": 43236.95, "cu