citation returned unexecuted 06/05/2023; subsequently served by posting. Ronald A. Williams Sr., Gloria V. Williams, and Chester F. Williams locations unknown; served by citation by posting 07/24/2023.','high','Insufficient data in docket text to determine complexity - appears to be loading page only','2026-01-07','JUDGMENT NON-JURY','2026-01-07',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas','/Users/stephenlewis/Downloads/pcpeak_platform/data/pdfs/TX-23-00569/petition.pdf','[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 12923.83}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 14493.29}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 5962.19}, {"entity": "Dallas County School Equalization Fund", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 393.2}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 71772.83}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 42824.18}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Internal Use Only**\n**Case:** TX-23-00569 | **Property:** 1506 Harbor Road, Dallas, TX\n**Prepared by:** Senior Acquisition Analyst | **Date:** July 2025\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is a **1950-built, 2,230 sq ft residential structure** sitting on a Cedar Crest Village lot (Block G/6075, 4th Section) with DCAD-recorded **50% depreciation**, placing the improvement at or near the end of its conventional economic life at 76 years old. The $286,730 market value needs to be interrogated against that depreciation figure: if DCAD is assigning meaningful improvement value to a structure this aged and this deteriorated, the **true market utility likely skews toward a land/teardown play** rather than a rehab-and-hold structure play. Cedar Crest Village is a south Dallas neighborhood with active infill development pressure, which supports a land-value thesis. The absence of a homestead exemption is a hard signal — this property is **not owner-occupied and has not been for years**, meaning no one is maintaining it with personal attachment or urgency. Ownership is vested in **"WILLIAMS CHESTER F EST OF"** at 100%, which tells us Chester F. Williams is deceased and the property is being held inside an unresolved estate — a classic title complexity trap. The payment history confirms Chester paid through **2020**, after which the estate went completely dark. Paula E. Williams paid in **1992 and 1993**, suggesting she was the occupant or responsible party three decades ago but has had no financial engagement with this asset since. The deed transfer date of **11/11/1900** appearing in DCAD is almost certainly a data artifact from the volume/page deed reference (Volume 67, Page 1638), not a literal conveyance date, but it flags that no clean modern transfer has been recorded — the estate has never been formally administered or conveyed out of Chester''s name. **This is a fractured estate play, not a straightforward individual seller situation.**\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nThe **live tax balance of $196,082.74** against a $286,730 DCAD market value produces a **debt-to-value ratio of 68.4%** — dangerously deep for any acquisition math. This is not a situation where the taxing authority is holding a modest lien; they are holding a **superpriority claim equal to more than two-thirds of assessed value**. What makes this more punishing is the penalty acceleration structure','\n',char(10)),'','oos_issued',286730.0,226910.24999999998001,'2026-06-02','2026-05-12','2026-06-12T14:33:24.445325','2026-07-09 05:04:50','2026-07-08T19:17:02.328556',1,'individual','high','Lot 1, in Block G/6075 of Cedar Crest Village, 4th Section, an Addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed w/Vendor''s Lien recorded in Volume 67 Page 1638 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','{"account_number": "00000503698000000", "market_