 property approximately 6–7 years. Based on DCAD records for this vintage of Garland 75041 stock, the improvement is likely a 1,200–1,800 SF masonry or frame/brick veneer construction, built in the 1960s to mid-1970s, placing the structure at 50–60 years of age with significant effective age depreciation baked into any DCAD cost-approach valuation. For accounts in this corridor of West Ridgewood Drive, DCAD typically carries improvement values in the $90,000–$130,000 range against land values of $25,000–$40,000, yielding an improvement-to-total ratio of approximately 70–80%. That ratio matters here: this is not a land play. The dirt alone won''t carry your basis. This is a **structure play** — the value thesis requires the improvement to be habitable or cost-effectively rehabable. The fact that taxes went delinquent beginning tax year 2023 (three consecutive years: 2023, 2024, 2025) is a meaningful behavioral signal. This was not a one-year oversight. Rivera Martinez stopped paying right around the time post-COVID assessment increases hit Dallas County hardest, suggesting either a cash-flow break, a decision to stop investing in the property, or a pending disposition that stalled. The presence of **Ken My Luong** (683 E. Muirfield Road, Garland, 75044) as an in-rem-only defendant is the most structurally significant data point in this file: Luong holds either a prior deed interest, a lien, or a recorded instrument against the property that PBFCM is naming to extinguish — this is almost certainly a **seller-carry note, private mortgage','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01T23:57:12.499163','2026-07-08T19:27:48.356638','2026-07-08T19:27:48.356638',1,'individual','high','LOT 32, BLOCK 2, RIDGEWOOD ESTATES NO. 1 ADDITION, AKA 209 W RIDGEWOOD DRIVE, CITY OF GARLAND, TEXAS AS RECORDED IN INSTRUMENT 201900205392, OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS','',NULL,'https://courtsportal.dallascounty.org/DALLASPROD/DocumentViewer/Display?eid=52F775A84EFD7AE7F29C604799C3FE50&docTypeId=791&caseNum=TX-26-00992&locationId=219&caseId=0F35D5B15F62ACD68B3E30C78FF7BDB8&docType=PETITION&docName=ORIGINAL+PETITION&eventName=ORIGINAL+PETITION');
INSERT INTO cases VALUES(27,'TX-26-00993','160th District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2026-05-19','OPEN','TAX DELINQUENCY','ELIZABETH ORTALEJO','[{"name": "ELIZABETH ORTALEJO", "address": "1607 Denton Drive, Carrollton, TX 75006", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "Constable #4", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Primary defendant, in personam"}, {"name": "ALEX RAFAEL ORTALEJO ESPINO", "address": "1607 Denton Drive, Carrollton, TX 75006", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "Constable #4", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Co-defendant"}]','1607 N. Denton Drive, City of Carrollton, Texas',NULL,'65051925510190000','LGBS (Linebarger)','REECE, LINDA D.',4430.1499999999993661,2024,'[2024, 2025]',2,0,0,'[]',0,0,0,'Citations issued 05/26/2026 but both defendants remain unserved','low',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,0,'2027-01-27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "CARROLLTON-FARMERS BRANCH INDEPENDENT SCHOOL DISTRICT", "taxAmt": 2773.86, "penaltyInterest": 1306.29, "total": 4080.15}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development – Priority Foreclosure Analysis**\n\n**Case:** TX-26-00993 | **Property:** 1607 N. Denton Drive, Carrollton, TX 75006  \n**Analyst Date:** January 2027 | **Classification:** HIGH-PRIORITY STRUCTURE PLAY\n\n---\n\n## 1. PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is a **brand-new construction structure play** with critical distress indicators. DCAD shows a 2025-built, 4,524 sqft home with current market value of $603,860—a recently completed spec build or custom home. The property transferred via deed on 8/31/2023, suggesting Elizabeth Ortalejo acquired raw land or a lot during construction phase. The 0.3184-acre lot in Martha P. Green Survey (Abstract 519) indicates urban infill development in established North Carrollton corridor. **Critical red flag: NO homestead exemption** on a property this size signals either investment intent, rental failure, or immediate post-construction financial collapse. The owner paid 2024 taxes but defaulted on 2025—pointing to acute financial distress beginning late 2025, possibly related to construction loan maturation, failed sale, or tenant default. Alex Rafael Ortalejo Espino as co-defendant suggests spouse or family partnership. DCAD shows live tax balance of $0.00 despite the lawsuit claiming $4,430.15 owed—this means either recent partial payment that hasn''t updated court records, or DCAD lag. The structure-to-total value ratio is essentially 100% given the 2025 build date, making this purely a **structure value play** with minimal land-only fallback position.\n\n## 2. FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nThe filing amount of **$4,430.15** covers only two delinquency years (2024-2025) with CFBISD taxes dominating at $2,773.86 principal plus $1,306.29 in penalties/interest—a 47% penalty load indicating filing occurred approximately 12+ months after initial 2024 delinquency. However, DCAD live data shows **$0.00 current balance**, creating a critical intelligence gap: either Ortalejo made payment post-filing (May 2026 or later) that satisfied the taxing authorities but Linebarger continues pursuing legal fees/costs, or DCAD hasn''t synchronized with court records. Assuming the debt is actually satisfied at taxing entity level, the **live payoff cost today** would be minimal legal fees (estimate $2,000-$3,500 in Linebarger attorney fees','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01T23:57:56.120068','2026-07-09 05:04:51','2026-07-07T12:41:10.054892',1,'individual','high','BEING 0.3184 ACRES, MORE OR LESS, TRACT 19, OF THE MARTHA P. GREEN SURVEY, ABSTRACT 519, PAGE 255, AKA 1607 N. DENTON DRIVE, CITY OF CARROLLTON, TEXAS AS RECORDED IN INSTRUMENT 202300177640, OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS','{"account_number": "65051925510190000", "market_value": 603860, "land_value": 100000, "improvement_value": 503860, "estimated_annual_taxes": 12196.01, "year_built": 2025, "effective_year_built": 2025, "actual_age": 1, "building_class": "21", "constructi