Status": "served", "serviceMethod": "substituted service Rule 106", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Citation issued 02/21/2023; served via Rule 106 substitute service; made default per judgment"}, {"name": "Cora Taylor Pride", "address": "unknown", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "private process server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Citation issued 02/21/2023; return unserved 05/30/2023"}, {"name": "Charlotte Ruth Winsett", "address": "unknown", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "private process server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Citation issued 02/21/2023; duly served per judgment; made default"}, {"name": "Mary Lucinda Hatley", "address": "unknown", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "attorney ad litem", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Unknown location; represented by attorney ad litem Mark W. Sutherland"}]','1522 East Waco Avenue, Dallas, TX',NULL,'00000279871000000','LGBS (Linebarger)','ATKINS, ASHLY STEELE',25227.669999999999816,2003,'[2003, 2004, 2005, 2006, 2007, 2008, 2009, 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024]',12,1,1,'[]',1,0,2,'Multiple defendants unserved by private process server; Annie Pearl Hatley cited by posting; Sherry Hatley Saddler served via Rule 106 substitute service; Larry Darnell Miles served via SOS; Mary Lucinda Hatley location unknown represented by attorney ad litem; Tony J. Hatley incarcerated at TDCJ; Bobby Charles Miles answered pro se','high','12 defendants (5+ triggers high complexity); multiple defendants with address unknown at filing requiring Citation by Posting; estate/heir situation evident from multiple family members and prior related 1984 suit; 20 years of delinquent taxes (2003-2022); out-of-state defendant requiring SOS service; incarcerated defendant; multiple ad litem appointments; Rule 106 substitute service needed; 3 continuances and 2 trial resets; judgment vacated requiring case reopening','2025-05-05','JUDGMENT NON-JURY','2025-05-05',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 2218.95}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 2468.62}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 1058.78}, {"entity": "Dallas County School Equalization Fund", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 69.14}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 12075.48}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 7336.7}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n## PC Peak Development | Senior Analyst Desk\n**Case:** TX-23-00244 | **Court:** 14th District Court | **Judge:** Ginsberg, Carl\n**Subject Property:** Dallas County | **Primary Defendant:** Hatley, Annie Pearl\n**Distress Score:** 9/10 — CRITICAL | **Classification:** HIGH PRIORITY ACQUISITION TARGET\n**Memo Date:** June 2025 | **Analyst:** Senior Acquisitions\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is almost certainly a **land play, not a structure play.** DCAD data flags improvement value as near zero, which in Dallas County context means one of three conditions: the structure has been demolished, condemned, or has depreciated to functional obsolescence with zero assessed contributory value. With no year-built data populating and no square footage on record, the working assumption is a vacant lot or a shell structure with no salvageable improvement value — the $81,000 market value is effectively land-only pricing, consistent with an infill lot in a Dallas submarket. The lot-to-improvement ratio here is essentially 100:0, which removes rehab math entirely and puts this squarely in the **land bank, new construction, or assemblage** bucket. The deed transferred on **3/2/2022**, meaning someone in this ownership group took a transaction-level action just 13 months before the tax suit was filed in February 2023 — that transfer may have been an estate distribution, quitclaim shuffle, or distressed conveyance, none of which suggests an engaged, equity-protective owner. The **absence of a homestead exemption** confirms no owner-occupant lives here; this is absentee, fragmented ownership. Payment history is the most telling signal: **Willie Joe Hatley paid taxes in 1999 and 2000 — 25 years ago** — and the record goes silent after that. That is not a missed payment or two; that is a complete generational disengagement from this asset. The current ownership vesting — **Miles Bobby et al. 70%, Martinez Delores Miles 15%, Miles Larry 15%** — reads like an intestate inheritance split or a quitclaim distribution among heirs of the original Hatley family, with the Miles surnames suggesting a separate family branch (possibly through marriage or adoption). The Hatley defendants (Annie Pearl, Willie Joe, Tony J., Tonette) and the Miles defendants (Bobby Charles, Larry Darnell, Delores Miles Martinez, Patricia Ann Camp) represent **two intertwined family trees**, none of whom appear to have maintained any financial relationship with this property in over two','\n',char(10)),NULL,'oos_issued',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-05T22:35:40.179547','2026-07-09 05:04:51','2026-07-08T19:15:31.399258',1,'individual','high','Lot 18, in Block 22/3583, Edgemont Addition No. 3, an addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed Without Vendor''s Lien recorded in Volume 69147, Page 1483 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','{"account_number": "00000279871000000", "market_value": 81000, "land_value": 81000, "improvement_value": 0, "estimated_annual_taxes": 1803.64, "year_built": null, "effective_year_built": null, "actual_age": null, "building_class": "", "construction_type": "", "foundation": "", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": null, "total_area_sqft": null, "bedrooms": null, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pc