2290.82, "total": 5399.43}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Tax Foreclosure Division**\n**Case No. TX-26-01376 | 3307 Fordham Rd., Dallas, TX 75216-4824**\n**Prepared:** July 2026 | **Analyst:** Senior Acquisitions | **Priority:** MODERATE\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe subject property is a 1,056 SF single-family residence constructed in 1970, now 56 years old and carrying a **50% depreciation flag** in DCAD''s system — meaning the improvement is assessed at or near the bottom half of its economic life cycle. At a DCAD market value of **$168,390**, the land-to-improvement ratio warrants close scrutiny: in the 75216 zip code (south Dallas, Bonnie View Gardens subdivision), lots of this vintage typically carry land values in the **$40,000–$60,000 range**, which would place the improvement value at approximately **$108,000–$128,000** on DCAD''s books. A structure this age, this size, and this depreciated in 75216 is not a structure play — **this is a hybrid land/teardown-or-light-rehab play**, with the primary value driver being the lot''s infill potential or wholesale-to-builder utility rather than any meaningful improvement preservation. The legal description anchors to Instrument No. 201300060575 in Dallas County Deed Records, a 2013 warranty deed transfer that brought the Gonzalez ownership interest into title. Critically, the deed and DCAD records reflect **two distinct ownership streams**: Juan Fernando Gonzalez and Graciela Janet Hernandez at the subject address (in personam defendants, almost certainly a married couple or co-habitating co-owners who acquired in 2013), and Micaela Acosta and Jose Acosta at 630 Delaware Ave, Dallas 75208 (in rem only defendants — prior lienholders or predecessor owners whose interest was never formally extinguished). The Acostas'' in-rem-only designation suggests a **title cloud from the 2013 acquisition**, likely a prior owner or seller who retained some recorded interest. The homestead exemption is active, confirming owner-occupied status as of the most recent tax year. Payment history is fractured and telling: names appearing as **JUAN GONZALEZ (paid 2025), JUAN F GONZALEZ (paid 2024), JOSELYN HERNANDEZ (paid 2024), and JUAN F GONALEZ (paid 2024)** across multiple years suggest either multiple','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T12:40:43.307906','2026-07-10T08:03:56.766264','2026-07-10T08:03:56.766264',1,'individual','high','Lot 9, in Block E, of the First Section of Bonnie View Gardens, an Addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded as Instrument Number 201300060575 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','{"account_number": "00000510040000000", "market_value": 168390, "land_value": 70000, "improvement_value": 98390, "estimated_annual_taxes": null, "year_built": 1970, "effective_year_built": 1970, "actual_age": 56, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "POST", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 1056, "total_area_sqft": 1056, "bedrooms": 3, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 50, "desirability": "AVERAGE", "air_condition": "CENTRAL FULL", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "", "lot_frontage_ft": null, "lot_depth_ft": null, "lot_area_sqft": null, "land_unit_price": null, "legal_description": "", "owners": [], "deed_transfer_date": "", "exemptions": "", "no_homestead": false, "tax_rates": [], "current_tax_balance": 18346.13, "current_levy": 3682.88, "prior_year_due": 14709.26, "payment_history": [{"date": "2026-05-08", "amount": 200.0, "tax_year": "2025", "payer": "JUAN GONZALEZ"}, {"date": "2026-04-24", "amount": 200.0, "tax_year": "2025", "payer": "JUAN GONZALEZ"}, {"date": "2026-03-16", "amount": 200.0, "tax_year": "2025", "payer": "JUAN GONZALEZ"}, {"date": "2026-02-20", "amount": 200.0, "tax_year": "2025", "payer": "JUAN GONZALEZ"}, {"date": "20