7}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development — Tax Foreclosure Analysis**\n**Case No. TX-26-01374 | 3203 Utah Avenue, Dallas, TX 75216**\n**Prepared by: Senior Acquisitions | Date: July 2026 | Classification: Internal Use Only**\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe subject property is a 1,358 SF single-family residence constructed in 1948, now 78 years old and carrying a DCAD-assigned 50% depreciation factor — placing this structure squarely at or near the end of its economic life for lending and resale purposes. DCAD''s market value of **$194,810** must be interrogated carefully: at 78 years of age with 50% structural depreciation, the improvement itself likely contributes a relatively modest share of that valuation, suggesting the **bulk of market value is land-driven**, not structure-driven. Trinity Heights Annex, a mid-century Dallas subdivision in the 75216 zip code (Oak Cliff corridor), has seen lot values appreciate as infill pressure from the southern Dallas redevelopment push intensifies. This is fundamentally a **land play with a salvageable or demo-ready structure** — the 1948 construction means original wiring, original plumbing stack, pier-and-beam or early slab foundation, and likely zero updates to mechanicals without documentation. Do not underwrite this as a turnkey rehab. The absence of any homestead exemption on DCAD confirms **Martha Rivers is not residing at the property** — she is either absentee landlord, has vacated, or the property sits vacant entirely. This is a critical distress signal.\n\nOwnership history is telling. The deed transfer date of **6/8/2000** in Volume 72144, Page 0081 references a Special Warranty Deed — not a general warranty deed — which signals the grantor at time of transfer was limiting their liability representation, often seen in estate transfers, distressed sales, or tax deed conveyances. DCAD shows **RIVERS MARTHA** as 100% owner of record, but the foreclosure petition names four defendants: Edward Brown Sr., Eva Mae Brown, Martha Rivers, and John Will Brown. This multi-defendant structure almost certainly reflects an **intestate or informal estate situation** — the Browns are likely heirs or prior owners with retained interest claims, and Martha Rivers may have inherited or received the property through a family chain without a clean probate. The payment history confirms: **Texas Tax Solution II LLC paid 2019** (a third-party tax lender — meaning someone previously took out a TPTL loan to cure delinqu','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T12:42:53.818902','2026-07-10T08:01:29.229204','2026-07-10T08:01:29.229204',1,'individual','high','Being Lot 13, in Block 21/5999 of Trinity Heights Annex, an addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Special Warranty Deed recorded in Volume 72144 Page 0081 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas.','{"account_number": "00000477631000000", "market_value": 194810, "land_value": 85000, "improvement_value": 109810, "estimated_annual_taxes": 4337.85, "year_built": 1948, "effective_year_built": 1948, "actual_age": 78, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "PIER AND BEAM", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 1358, "total_area_sqft": 1358, "bedrooms": 3, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 50, "desirability": "AVERAGE", "air_condition": "WINDOW", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "SINGLE FAMILY 7500 SQFT", "lot_frontage_ft": 60, "lot_depth_ft": 173, "lot_area_sqft": 10152.0, "land_unit_price": 85000.0, "legal_description": "1: TRINITY HEIGHTS ANNEX 2: BLK 21/5999 LT 13 3: 4: VOL2000113/3422 DD05032000 CO-DC 5: 5999 021 01300 4DA5999 021 Deed Transfer Date: 6/8/2000", "owners": [{"name": "RIVERS MARTHA", "pct": 100}], "deed_transfer_date": "6/8/2000", "exemptions": "None", "no_homestead": true, "tax_rates": [], "current_tax_balance": 19175.83, "current