*86 years of age** with DCAD-assessed depreciation at **45%** — meaning the structure itself has shed nearly half its contributory value on paper, and likely more in functional reality. At 951 square feet with major mechanical systems (roof, HVAC, plumbing, electrical) well past typical useful life thresholds, this is **primarily a land play with a teardown-or-heavy-rehab structure overlay**. The lot — described as the east 50 feet of Lot 84, Urbandale Addition First Installment — carries the bulk of the economic value. DCAD pegs total market at **$191,720**, and given the age/size/depreciation profile, the improvement contribution is likely no more than $40,000–$55,000 of that figure, meaning raw land value in the 75227 submarket is doing the heavy lifting here. No homestead exemption is on file, which is a critical signal: Ramos is **not occupying this property** as a primary residence. The deed transferred into Ramos''s name on **January 14, 2003** — he has held this asset for over 23 years — but the absence of homestead suggests he is either renting it, holding it vacant, or has relocated entirely. His listed address on the citation (**6336 Everglade Rd., Dallas, TX 75227**) is a separate parcel approximately 1.2 miles away in the same zip, consistent with an absentee landlord profile within the same neighborhood. Payment history tells a fragmented story: multiple name variants appear across 2021 payments — **Maria Villagran, Maria Ran, Maria V, Fernando Ramos** — suggesting either a tenant-assisted payment arrangement, a family member managing the account informally, or prior clouded ownership with informal occupancy. Ramos himself paid **2023 and 2024** directly, skipped **2022**, then the 2021 year remained disputed across','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T22:58:23.194743','2026-07-09 05:04:53','2026-07-08T20:41:42.859386',1,'individual','high','Being more or less 50 feet off east side of Lot 84 of First Installment of Urband