{"entity": "City of Dallas (Tract 2)", "taxAmt": 1236.74, "penaltyInterest": 737.05, "total": 1973.79}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development — Internal Use Only**\n**Case:** TX-26-01196 | **Property:** 3625 & 3635 Crane St., Dallas, TX 75212\n**Prepared by:** Acquisitions Analytics Desk | **Date:** June 2026\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis case involves **two adjacent parcels** — Lots 4A and 4C in Block 7/7151, Homeland Estates Revised Addition — located on Crane Street in the **75212 zip code (West Dallas / Westmoreland Hills corridor)**. DCAD data signals a near-zero improvement value relative to the $57,000 combined market value assessment, which is the most important structural fact in this file: **this is a land play, not a structure play.** The improvement value approaching zero strongly indicates the parcels are either vacant lots, have a demolished or condemned structure, or contain a structure so deteriorated it contributes negligible assessed value. No homestead exemption is on file, confirming the property is either absentee-owned or investor-held — Gayla Jefferson is not living here. The legal defendant, **Gayla Jefferson**, carries a listed address of **1467 E. Highland Rd., Waxahachie, TX 75167** — approximately 35 miles south of the subject parcels — reinforcing the absentee ownership profile. The deed records are worth flagging: the legal description references a Warranty Deed recorded in **Volume 2000207, Page 577** of Dallas County Deed Records, suggesting the chain of title has been around for some time, yet DCAD currently shows ownership under **ANDERSON BETTY (100%)**. This is a material discrepancy — the tax suit names Jefferson as defendant, while DCAD reflects Anderson as current owner of record following a **deed transfer dated 4/26/2023**. This could mean Jefferson conveyed to Anderson post-delinquency, potentially in a quitclaim or distressed transfer, and Linebarger/LGBS is pursuing Jefferson as the liable party for pre-transfer delinquencies. This ownership gap requires immediate deed chain verification through Dallas County Clerk records. Delinquency runs **2022–2025** — four consecutive years — indicating total abandonment of tax obligation and zero engagement with the taxing authorities across multiple fiscal cycles. The distress score of 5/HIGH is warranted.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nThe **total filed amount at suit initiation (June 16, 2026) is $12,598.68**, spanning both Tract ','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T23:27:58.984717','2026-07-09 05:04:56','2026-07-08T20:52:39.720651',1,'individual','high','Lots 4C and 4A in Block 7/7151, Homeland Estates Revised Addition, an Addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded in Volume 2000207 Page 577 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','{"account_number": "00000685651000000, 00000685645000000", "market_value": 114000, "land_value": 114000, "improvement_value": 0, "estimated_annual_taxes": 2538.44, "year_built": null, "effective_year_built": null, "actual_age": null, "building_class": "", "construction_type": "", "foundation": "", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": null, "total_area_sqft": null, "bedrooms": null, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": null, "desirability": "", "air_condition": "", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "SINGLE FAMILY 5K SQFT", "lot_frontage_ft": 50, "lot_depth_ft": 120, "lot_area_sqft": 12191.0, "land_unit_price": 95000.0, "legal_description": "1: HOMELAND ESTATES REVISED 2: BLK 7/7151 LT 4C 3: 4: VOL84211 PG 2200 DD08251987 CO-DC 5: 7151 007 04C00 2007151 007 Deed Transfer Date: 4/26/2023", "owners": [{"name": "ANDERSON BETTY", "pct": 100}], "deed_transfer_date": "4/26/2023", "exemptions": "None", "no_homestead": true, "tax_rates": [], "current_tax_balance": 12818.779999999999, "current_levy": 2538.48, "pri