 MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Internal Use Only**\n**Case:** TX-26-01197 | **Property:** 10555 Barrywood Drive, Dallas, TX 75230\n**Prepared by:** Senior Acquisitions Analyst | **Date:** June 2026\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe subject property is a 1,989 SF single-family residence built in 1970 in the Crestmeadow Estates subdivision (Block M/7288, Lot 24), sitting on a Dallas County-appraised market value of **$455,100**. At 56 years old with a **45% depreciation factor** applied by DCAD, the structure itself carries significant wear — this is not a turnkey asset. The improvement-to-land ratio in the 75230 ZIP code (a transitional Preston Hollow-adjacent corridor) is critical here: if land value is carrying the bulk of that $455K appraisal, this is fundamentally a **land play or heavy-rehab play**, not a structure play. A 1970-vintage 1,989 SF home at 45% depreciation in this market likely reflects a land value floor in the **$300K–$340K range**, with the structure contributing a depreciated improvement value of roughly **$115K–$155K** — meaning the dirt is doing the work. Investors acquiring in this corridor are largely buying for lot value, teardown/rebuild potential, or significant gut-rehab to bring the asset up to neighborhood comps.\n\nOwnership history reveals a nuanced chain of title and payment behavior. **LVS Second Homes LLC** held title and was current through tax year 2021 — an entity registered at 9241 LBJ Freeway, Suite 100, Dallas, TX 75243, with Andrew H. Schultz as registered agent, suggesting a professional real estate holding structure. The LLC conveyed the property to **George Sidiq Bility** via Warranty Deed recorded as Instrument No. 202200211422 in 2022. Bility paid 2022 taxes (appearing in DCAD records under three name variations: GEORGE SIDIQ BILITY, GEORGE BILITY, and BILITY GEORGE SIDIQ — likely data entry inconsistencies, not separate parties), but the property went **fully delinquent beginning 2022 and extending t