t at **42–48 years of effective age**. At that age bracket, DCAD typically applies a depreciation schedule that reduces improvement value to 35–55% of replacement cost new, meaning the land component is carrying a disproportionate share of total assessed value relative to a newer structure. This is a **hybrid play** — the lot itself in Garland''s 75040 zip code holds genuine intrinsic value (typically assessed land value in this subdivision runs $35,000–$55,000), but the improvement likely still clears $120,000–$145,000 DCAD assessed value, making the total appraised value range approximately **$155,000–$200,000**. The key structural risk is deferred maintenance: homes in this age-and-income corridor, when tax delinquent, frequently present with HVAC systems beyond service life (15+ years), original cast-iron drain lines with root intrusion, and roofs that have been patched rather than replaced. This is **not a teardown land play** — Garland does not support new construction economics on a single interior lot at this price point — so any offer must account for renovation budget as a real cost variable. The defendant, **Sopanna Sengmany**, holds title as an individual and the property address matches the defendant''s listed address, strongly suggesting this is an **owner-occupied** or **recently owner-occupied** situation, not an absentee landlord. The presence of **Portfolio Recovery Associates, LLC** (In Rem Only) as the second defendant is the critical ownership complexity here: PRA is a major debt-buyer, and their lien is almost certainly an old **consumer credit','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T07:39:31.357300','2026-07-10T07:39:31.357300','2026-07-10T07:39:31.357300',1,'individual','high','LOT 37, BLOCK 10, BUCKINGHAM VILLAGE ESTATES NO. 3 ADDITION, AKA 2221 PHOENIX DRIVE, CITY OF GARLAND, TEXAS AS RECORDED IN VOLUME 2004117, PAGE 4623, OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS','',NULL,NULL);
