Clerk''s File No. 201500306518; serve Hon. Ken Paxton AG"}]','1224 Gonzales Drive, Mesquite, TX 75150-4288',NULL,'381208100E0070000','LGBS (Linebarger)','ZOKAIE, CHEYENNE MATHEW',26054.699999999999526,2023,'[2023, 2024, 2025]',8,1,0,'[]',1,0,0,'Two defendants (Theresa L. Quinlan and Shannon Lynne Sherman) have unknown addresses; Citation by Posting requested and CBP affidavits filed 07/08/2026. All citations unserved as of docket. Attorney Ad Litem appointed 07/08/2026.','high',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,0,'2027-03-01',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 1198.87, "penaltyInterest": 524.44, "total": 1723.31}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 1179.4, "penaltyInterest": 515.92, "total": 1695.32}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 590.12, "penaltyInterest": 257.82, "total": 847.94}, {"entity": "Mesquite Independent School District", "taxAmt": 7374.24, "penaltyInterest": 3879.18, "total": 11253.42}, {"entity": "City of Mesquite", "taxAmt": 6959.02, "penaltyInterest": 3575.69, "total": 10534.71}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n## PC Peak Development | TX-26-01371\n**Prepared by:** Senior Acquisitions Analyst\n**Date:** July 2026\n**Property:** [Subject Property – DCAD Pull Required]\n**Classification:** HIGH COMPLEXITY | FRAGMENTED OWNERSHIP | CITATION BY POSTING\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe DCAD record on this property will be the first pull before any contact is made, but the case structure itself tells a significant story before we ever see a square footage number. The lead defendant, **Theresa L. Quinlan**, has a current address listed as **"Address Unknown"** — with a Citation by Posting (CBP) affidavit already filed on **07/08/2026**, just two days after the case was filed on 07/06/2026. That speed of CBP filing suggests the taxing authority already exhausted conventional location attempts, meaning Quinlan has been functionally absent from the property for a material period of time. The CBP route is not a casual election — it signals the county attorney''s office had zero forwarding address to work with. This dramatically increases the probability of **vacancy, abandonment, or estate fragmentation**. The presence of **six additional named defendants** — Shannon Lynne Sherman, Cody Ray Quinlan, Samantha Lynne Tinney, Dillion Scott Hiberd, Dakota Wayne Forrester, and Savannah Lee Sanchez — across addresses in Mesquite, Weatherford, Millsap, Springtown, and Hudson Oaks is the clearest structural signal in this file: **this is a fractured heir or extended-family ownership situation**, not a clean single-owner delinquency. The geographic dispersion of defendants across Parker, Wise, and Dallas counties, combined with the Quinlan surname appearing twice (Theresa and Cody), strongly suggests a **generational transfer that was never probated or formally titled**, leaving the property in a legal gray zone that deterred tax payments. On the physical side — pending full DCAD pull — the presence of this many defendants and the CBP filing pattern is consistent with properties that are **older vintage (pre-1980 construction)**, have a **high land-to-improvement value ratio** (meaning the structure itself has depreciated substantially while the dirt has held or appreciated), and have seen deferred maintenance for years. If DCAD returns an improvement value below 40% of total assessed value, this is a **land play with a tear-down or heavy rehab structure on top**. If improvement value is 50–65% of total assessed, it may support a gut-rehab acquisition strategy.','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T07:58:07.288724','2026-07-10T07:58:07.288724','2026-07-10T07:58:07.288724',1,'individual','high','Being Lot 7, Block E, of Meadowview Farms No. 2, an Addition in the City of Mesquite, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Affidavit of Heirship recorded as Instrument Number 202200256856 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','',NULL,NULL);
