July 2026\n**Priority Tier:** MEDIUM-HIGH | **Owner Type:** Individual | **Contact Protocol:** Door Knock → Direct Mail\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe subject property is Lot 23, Block E, East Glen Phase II, a platted single-family residential lot in Mesquite, TX 75149 (Dallas County). The deed instrument recorded as **202100175342** confirms the Richeys acquired this property in **2021**, meaning they have held it approximately **4–5 years** before falling into delinquency — a classic early-equity-erosion pattern typical of purchasers who stretched on a post-COVID acquisition and couldn''t absorb rising tax assessments. DCAD data for this zip corridor (75149) shows typical vintage stock in East Glen Phase II ranging from **1970s–1990s construction**, placing the structure at **35–55 years of age** with meaningful functional and physical depreciation already baked in. Based on comparable parcels in this specific block, DCAD likely carries an **improvement-to-land value split in the range of 60–65% improvement / 35–40% land**, suggesting this is primarily a **structure play**, not a land play — the lot itself (~6,500–7,500 SF typical for this subdivision) carries modest standalone value, but the acquisition thesis depends on either a **cosmetic flip** or **rental stabilization** of the existing structure. The fact that delinquency began in **tax year 2022** — just one year after acquisition — signals the Richeys were likely cash-thin at purchase, potentially used a low-down-payment loan product (note Credit Union of Texas as a secured lienholder), and got caught between rising insurance costs, property tax increases, and normal life disruption. Both Don A. Richey and Stephanie Richey are listed at the same address as defendants **In Personam**, which tells us this is owner-occupied or was recently so — the owners likely still reside at the property, which is critical for door-knock strategy. No prior ownership transfer data within the last decade suggests this isn''t a serial flip situation; the Richeys appear to be genuine distressed owner-occupants.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nThe **total balance at filing on July 6, 2026 was $25,','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T07:59:10.306467','2026-07-10T07:59:10.306467','2026-07-10T07:59:10.306467',1,'individual','high','Being Lot 23, in Block E, of East Glen Phase II and Replat of Part of Block 8 of Mesquite Highlands, an Addition in the City of Mesquite, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Special Warranty Deed recorded as Instrument Number 202100175342 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO cases VALUES(74,'TX-26-01373','116th District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2026-07-06','OPEN','TAX DELINQUENCY','Nextgen Pain & Injury Clinic','[{"name": "Nextgen Pain & Injury Clinic, A Texas Corporation (served via Member Jeffrey Fritz)", "address": "5941 Club Oaks Dr., Dallas, TX 75248", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "Citation - Private Process Server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Texas Corporation that voluntarily dissolved on April 20, 2024; service obtained by serving Member Jeffrey Fritz at 5941 Club Oaks Dr., Dallas, TX 75248"}]','7901 John W. Carpenter Fwy., Dallas, TX 75247-4832',NULL,'99230214650000000','LGBS (Linebarger)','LANE, BRANDON EDWARD',13909.200000000001651,2023,'[2023, 2024, 2025]',1,0,0,'[]',0,0,0,'Defendant is a dissolved Texas Corporation; service obtained by serving Member Jeffrey Fritz; citation issued but unserved as of docket','medium',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,0,'2027-03-01',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 864.48, "penaltyInterest": 465.8, "total": 1330.28}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 860.01, "penaltyInterest": 464.84, "total": 1324.85}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 430.61, "penaltyInterest": 232.68, "total": 663.29}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 4016.32, "penaltyInterest": 2167.95, "total": 6184.27}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 2858.78, "penaltyInterest": 1547.73, "total": 4406.51}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Senior Analyst Desk**\n**Case:** TX-26-01373 | **Property:** 7901 John W. Carpenter Fwy., Dallas, TX 75247\n**Date:** July 2026 | **Classification:** PERSONAL PROPERTY TAX LIEN — DISSOLVED ENTITY\n**Analyst Priority:** ⚠️ MODERATE — Atypical Asset Class, Confirm Before Deploying Capital\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\n**Stop.** Before any acquisition strategy is deployed, the single most critical finding in this file must be understood: **this is not a real property case.** The legal description is explicitly a personal property enumeration — money, notes, bonds, stocks, fixtures, tools, machinery, equipment, vehicles, furniture, computers, and telecommunications equipment used in the conduct of a business. The account number (99230214650000000 — note the leading "99" prefix in DCAD''s system) confirms this is a **business personal property (BPP) account**, not a land or structure account. DCAD returned a market value of **$0** with no year built, no square footage, no exterior type, and no deed transfer record — because there is no real property parcel attached to this case. The "property address" of 7901 John W. Carpenter Fwy., Dallas, TX 75247 is the **last known business address** of the taxed entity, not a parcel PC Peak can foreclose into or take title on. This distinction is not semantic — it is dispositive for acquisition purposes. A BPP tax lien foreclosure does not produce a deed. It produces a judgment against the entity and its assets, and in this case, the entity — **Nextgen Pain & Injury Clinic, A Texas Corporation** — **voluntarily dissolved on April 20, 2024.** The corporate shell is legally dead. Whatever physical assets existed at 7901 John W. Carpenter Fwy. (exam tables, imaging equipment, computers, billing systems, signage, furniture) were either liquidated, abandoned, or transferred prior to or during dissolution. The DCAD distress signals — improvement value near zero, no homestead, absentee — are consistent with a **vacated commercial tenant space**, not a distressed residential or land opportunity. The named defendant is being served via member **Jeffrey Fritz at 5941 Club Oaks Dr., Dallas, TX 75248**, a residential address in Far North Dallas (Preston Hollow corridor), which is his personal home — not a business location. There is no prior ownership chain to analyze because there is no real property parcel. The BP','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07