INSERT INTO cases VALUES(76,'TX-25-02263','193rd District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2025-12-31','OPEN','TAX DELINQUENCY','P & F CUSTOM HOMES','[{"name": "P & F Custom Homes, A Texas Limited Liability Company (Manager: Jerry Wayne Freeny)", "address": "2428 Diamond Point, Cedar Hill, TX 75104", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "CITATION - PRIVATE PROCESS SERVER", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "LLC certification of organization forfeited August 20, 2021 for non-payment of franchise taxes. Service obtained via Manager Jerry Wayne Freeny. Served 02/05/2026."}]','2715 Alamain Drive, Dallas, TX 75241',NULL,'00000755308000000','LGBS (Linebarger)','RUSSELL, LAVONDA T.',3251.4499999999997292,2023,'[2023, 2024]',1,0,0,'[{"suitNo": "TX-11-32044", "style": "DALLAS COUNTY, ETAL VS. CURTIS LEE JONES, ETAL", "court": "193rd District Court"}]',0,0,0,'','low',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,0,'2026-09-28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 206.73, "penaltyInterest": 104.9, "total": 311.63}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 204.89, "penaltyInterest": 104.13, "total": 309.02}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 102.2, "penaltyInterest": 51.96, "total": 154.16}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 959.9, "penaltyInterest": 487.43, "total": 1447.33}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 682.36, "penaltyInterest": 346.95, "total": 1029.31}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development — Tax Foreclosure Analysis**\n**Case:** TX-25-02263 | **Property:** 2715 Alamain Drive, Dallas, TX 75241\n**Prepared By:** Senior Acquisition Analyst | **Date:** Current\n**Classification:** HIGH DISTRESS — ACTIVE PURSUIT\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is almost certainly a **land play, not a structure play.** DCAD data shows improvement value near zero against a $75,000 market value, which in the Alta Mesa Park Estates context strongly indicates either a demolished structure, a never-built vacant lot, or a stripped shell with no assessable improvement remaining. The legal description confirms a single lot — Lot 6, Block 6/7614 of Alta Mesa Park Estates Third Installment — a post-WWII subdivision platted in south Dallas (75241 zip), a corridor that has seen significant abandonment, teardowns, and land banking activity over the past two decades. No year-built data, no square footage, no exterior construction type in DCAD further confirms the improvement is functionally non-existent for valuation purposes. The $75,000 market value is therefore almost entirely land value, and the depreciation figure is irrelevant — there is nothing structural to depreciate. This is raw or effectively raw infill dirt in a low-income south Dallas submarket adjacent to I-20, worth pursuing purely as a hold-and-build or wholesale lot play.\n\nThe ownership chain is the most important intelligence in this file. **P & F Custom Homes, LLC** acquired via deed transfer on **4/20/2017** — that eight-year hold with no development and no homestead exemption signals a stalled spec builder who bought with intent to build, never executed, and is now carrying dead weight. More critically, the LLC''s **certificate of formation was forfeited by the Texas Secretary of State on August 20, 2021** for non-payment of franchise taxes, meaning P & F Custom Homes has been operating as a legally dead entity for nearly four years. The manager, **Jerry Wayne Freeny**, is the only person with authority to act, and he was personally served on **02/05/2026** via private process server at **2428 Diamond Point, Cedar Hill, TX 75104** — a residential address suggesting Freeny is an individual operating a now-defunct small builder out of his home. The payment history adds a revealing wrinkle: taxes were paid in 2023, 2024, and 2025 by **Tracy Davis Freeny** — almost certainly Jerry''s spouse or family member — indicating someone in the Freeny','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'20