ng''s contributory value. At 101 years old, the structure has almost certainly exhausted its economic useful life: original plumbing, knob-and-tube or early Romex electrical, pier-and-beam foundation with likely differential settlement, and zero evidence of permitted renovation in the tax record. The absence of an exterior material designation in the DCAD data is a red flag — it often signals a structure too deteriorated or non-standard to categorize cleanly, or data that was never updated because no inspection was warranted. At $177,080 market value on a 792 sq ft footprint, the **land is carrying this asset**, not the improvements. Run the lot-to-improvement ratio: if DCAD''s improvement value is sitting at or below $30,000–$45,000 (consistent with 50% depreciation on a 1925 structure of this size), then land accounts for **75–85% of total assessed value** — confirming this is a teardown or gut-rehab land acquisition.\n\nOwnership is held as **"Johnson, Jasper Est. Of"** — an estate, not a living individual — which immediately tells us Jasper Johnson is deceased and **no probate has been filed or completed**, otherwise title would have transferred. The deed last changed hands on **9/15/2014**, over a decade ago. The defendant roster is a fragmented heir pool: Jasper Johnson (deceased), Helen Johnson (likely spouse or sibling), Lewis A. Johnson, James Weldon Johnson, Calvin Harris II (in rem only, likely a lienholder or heir by a different surname), Paula Ann Hines (in rem only, personal address obtained — 5230 Darlene St., Dallas 75232), and Viola M. Thomas (in rem only, 520 Smokey Trl., Glenn Heights 75154). The **payment history is the most revealing data point in this file**: Viola Thomas paid','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T10:36:38.111276','2026-07-10T10:36:38.111276','2026-07-10T10:36:38.111276',1,'individual','high','Being part of Lot 1 less DART in Block 3/3868 of Cedar Cliff Addition, an addition in the City of Dallas, 