*, and at least five Killough family members — Floyd Jefferson Killough, Shirley May Killough Rollins, Dennis Olin Killough, Floyd Duane Killough, Jimmy Don Killough, Rodney Henry Killough, Mary Olinda Dresser (née Killough, presumably) — all carry an ownership or heir interest. The homestead exemption, still active, is almost certainly a **stale filing** that was never removed after the original occupant (Henry Olin, Sr.) died or vacated — a common scenario in Texas heir-property situations that Dallas CAD frequently fails to audit. Henry Olin Killough as primary defendant has address listed as **unknown**, and the affidavit for citation by posting filed **01/05/2','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T10:38:06.199685','2026-07-10T10:38:06.199685','2026-07-10T10:38:06.199685',1,'individual','high','Being a 1.406 acs, more or less, Ann Arbor & Veterans in the Felix Sadler Survey, Abstract No. 1378, now in City Block 5144, Lot C, in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded in Volume 75094 Page 78 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','{"account_number": "00000363385000000", "market_value": 131810, "land_value": 131810, "improvement_value": 0, "estimated_annual_taxes": null, "year_built": null, "effective_year_built": null, "actual_age": null, "building_class": "", "construction_type": "", "foundation": "", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": null, "total_area_sqft": null, "bedrooms": null, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": null, "desirability": "", "air_condition": "", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "", "lot_frontage_ft": null, "lot_depth_ft": null, "lot_area_sqft": null, "land_unit_price": null, "legal_description": "", "owners": [], "deed_transfer_date": "", "exemptions": "", "no_homestead": false, "tax_rates": [], "current_tax_balance": 15606.57, "current_levy": 2028.71, "prior_year_due": 12733.91, "payment_history