for reappraisal, or a tear-down-grade improvement that appraisers are depreciating toward land value. Given the 75230 corridor''s lot premiums (Preston Hollow-adjacent lots routinely trade at **$35–$55/sqft**), this is almost certainly a **land play or lot-value-dominant play**, not a structure play. If the lot runs a standard **7,500–10,000 sqft** for this neighborhood vintage, raw land value alone likely anchors in the **$180K–$280K range**, meaning the improvement may be contributing minimal or negative value to the DCAD assessment — a classic teardown profile. The ownership chain tells a specific story: **CAPITAL TITLE OF TEXAS LLC** appears in 2021 (likely a closing/title holding entity, not an end investor), **ASHRAF DEIRI** paid taxes through 2024 suggesting hands-on ownership, and **MECCA FA INVESTMENTS LLC** received a deed transfer on **02/12/2026** — just **49 days before this memo date** and notably *after* the lawsuit was filed on **12/30/2025**. That post-suit deed transfer is the single most important data point in this file. It suggests either a distressed flip attempt, an internal restructuring among related parties (Saad → Mecca FA), or a deliberate title-clouding maneuver to complicate the foreclosure. The absence of a **homestead exemption** confirms this is investor-held, non-owner-occupied property. No emotional attachment. Pure financial exposure.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 —','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T10:39:32.907920','2026-07-10T10:39:32.907920','2026-07-10T10:39:32.907920',1,'individual','high','Being Lot 7-A in Block 7 of William Carter, Jr. Subdivision, an addition in the City of Mesquite, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded as Instrument Number 202100285523 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','{"account_number": "38019500070070000", "market_value": 267600, "land_value": 42740, "improvement_value": 224860, "estimated_annual_taxes": 6277.0, "year_built": null, "effective_year_