00000680158000000','LGBS (Linebarger)','RUSSELL, LAVONDA T.',33241.760000000000196,2020,'[2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024]',7,1,0,'[]',1,0,0,'Liza Joe Baker and Lila Virginia Baker addresses unknown — Citation by Posting issued 01/07/2026, served 02/16/2026; Cynthia F. Baker and Joe Lawrence Diamond III returned unserved 01/29/2026; attorney ad litem appointed 01/08/2026 for unknown-address defendants','high',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 1763.55, "penaltyInterest": 1234.32, "total": 2997.87}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 1862.61, "penaltyInterest": 1321.9, "total": 3184.51}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 911.48, "penaltyInterest": 642.89, "total": 1554.37}, {"entity": "Dallas County School Equalization Fund", "taxAmt": 42.83, "penaltyInterest": 36.56, "total": 79.39}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 8979.87, "penaltyInterest": 6406.49, "total": 15386.36}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 5905.67, "penaltyInterest": 4133.59, "total": 10039.26}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Senior Analyst Desk**\n**Case:** TX-25-02238 | **Subject Property:** [Address on file – DCAD pull required] | **Date:** June 2025\n**Defendant:** BAKER, LIZA JOE | **Court:** 134th District Court | **Judge:** Ginsberg, Carl\n**Classification:** HIGH DISTRESS | **Priority Tier:** ACTIVE PURSUIT\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is a **structure play with land optionality**, not a pure land acquisition. The subject is a 1,062 sq ft single-family residence built in 1962 — now 63 years old — carrying DCAD-assessed depreciation of 45%, which is a hard signal that the physical asset is significantly worn, likely suffering from deferred maintenance across mechanical systems, roof, and envelope. At $270,300 in market value against a structure this age and size, the land is doing meaningful lifting here; Dallas land values in this corridor are absorbing much of that number, which means if the structure is functionally obsolete or unlivable, a rehab-to-rent or tear-down-to-rebuild path both remain viable. The lot-to-improvement value ratio should be confirmed on DCAD, but given 45% depreciation on a 63-year-old structure, expect improvements to represent **under $90,000–$100,000** of the assessed value, with land carrying **$170,000+**. The absence of a homestead exemption is a definitive signal: **this property is not owner-occupied**. It is either vacant, tenant-occupied, or abandoned — all of which are consistent with the "Address Unknown" service posture for Liza Joe Baker (primary defendant) and the Citation by Posting method used to serve her. The ownership record reads **BAKER LILA LIFE ESTATE 100%**, which tells us Lila Virginia Baker held a life estate with remainder interest distributing to heirs — almost certainly the Baker family defendants listed in this case. The deed transfer date of 11/11/1900 in DCAD is a data artifact or placeholder, not literal, but it does suggest the chain of title has not been formally updated in decades, consistent with generational family ownership and estate fragmentation. Payment history reveals a clear disengagement pattern: **Mark Baker paid 2019**, **Lila Life Estate paid 2020**, and then — nothing. Three consecutive years of non-payment following what appears to be the death or incapacitation of the life estate holder. This is a classic **heir fragmentation scenario**: the life estate holder is gone or','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T10:41:04.374574','2026-07-10T10:41:04.374574','2026-07-10T10:41:04.374574',1,'individual','high','Being the East 30 feet of Lot 14, and the West 20 feet of Lot 15 in Block 29/7127, of Victory Gardens No. 5 Sec 2, an addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded in Volume 4431 Page 14 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas.'