, "taxAmt": 3276.77, "penaltyInterest": 2091.96, "total": 5368.73}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 2216.37, "penaltyInterest": 1395.84, "total": 3612.21}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Texas Tax Foreclosure Division**\n**Case No. TX-25-02240 | 160th District Court | Judge Carl Ginsberg**\n**Subject Property: 3147 McDermott Ave., Dallas, TX 75215**\n**Prepared: June 2026 | Analyst: Senior Acquisitions**\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is a **land play, not a structure play.** The improvement is a 756 sq/ft wood-frame residence constructed in 1924 — 102 years old — carrying a **60% depreciation factor** per DCAD, which signals the structure is functionally obsolete and near the end of its economic life. At $84,550 total market value, DCAD''s internal valuation almost certainly places the majority of that figure in the land, with improvement value contributing minimally given the depreciation load. A 756 sq/ft structure this age on a 33-1/3 ft lot in the 75215 zip code (South Dallas/Liberty Place Addition) is unlikely to support renovation economics — rehab costs on a century-old frame home of this size routinely run $60K–$90K before profit margin exists. The absence of a homestead exemption is a critical signal: **this property is not owner-occupied**, and given the vesting reads "ALEXANDER OLLIE MAE EST OF," Ollie Mae Alexander is almost certainly deceased, leaving the property in a nominal estate with no active stewardship. The deed transferred in **January 1995** and has not moved since — over 30 years of single-family hold. Payment history reveals a fractured, multi-party pattern: **Shanta Peace** paid 2020 and 2021 taxes (a non-owner, possibly a tenant or informal occupant), **Ollie Mae Alexander** (the individual, pre-estate) paid in 2004, 2017, and 2020, and the **Estate** entity paid 2021. No payments have been recorded for 2022, 2023, or 2024 — a clean four-year delinquency run. The involvement of Shanta Peace as a prior payor who is not a named defendant and not a deed holder suggests there may have been an informal occupancy arrangement that has since collapsed. The property is almost certainly vacant or occupied by an unauthorized party. The acquisition target here is the **dirt** — Liberty Place Addition lots in this corridor have redevelopment interest tied to southern Dallas infill and affordable housing tax credit activity.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nAt filing on **December ','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T10:43:41.030049','2026-07-10T10:43:41.030049','2026-07-10T10:43:41.030049',1,'individual','high','Being the East 33-1/3 feet of Lot 16 in Block 1802 of Liberty Place Addition, an addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the General Warranty Deed recorded in Volume 95011 Page 4244 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas','{"account_number": "00000176998000000", "market_value": 84550, "land_value": 32140, "improvement_value": 52410, "estimated_annual_taxes": 1882.68, "year_built": 1924, "effective_year_built": 1924, "actual_age": 102, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "POST", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 756, "total_area_sqft": 756, "bedrooms": 1, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 60, "desirability": "FAIR", "air_condition": "WINDOW", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "PLANNED DEVELOPMENT DISTRICT", "lot_frontage_ft": 34, "lot_depth_ft": 100, "lot_area_sqft": 3214.0, "land_unit_price": 10.0, "legal_description": "1: BLK 1802 2: NE 33 1/3'' LT 16 3: 4: VOL95011/4244 DD122894 CO-DALLAS 5: 1802 000 01600 1001802 000 Deed Transfer Date: 1/17/1995", "owners": [{"name": "ALEXANDER OLLIE MAE EST OF", "pct": 100}], "deed_transfer_date": "1/17/1995", "exemptions": "None", "no_homestead": true, "tax_rates": [], "current_tax_balance": 15078.66, "current_levy": 1817.67, "p