y Ad Litem appointed 01/08/2026','high',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 847.47, "penaltyInterest": 487.77, "total": 1335.24}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 868.82, "penaltyInterest": 504.12, "total": 1372.94}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 431.7, "penaltyInterest": 250.2, "total": 681.9}, {"entity": "Dallas County School Equalization Fund", "taxAmt": 12.24, "penaltyInterest": 8.92, "total": 21.16}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 4156.72, "penaltyInterest": 2425.45, "total": 6582.17}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 2848.88, "penaltyInterest": 1646.15, "total": 4495.03}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Tax Foreclosure Division**\n**Case No. TX-25-02241 | 14th District Court | Judge Carl Ginsberg**\n**Property: 1715 Marfa Ave., Dallas, TX 75216 | Date: 2025**\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is a **land play with a distressed structure bonus**, not a structure preservation opportunity. The subject property is a 996 sq/ft single-family residence built in **1938**, now 88 years old, carrying **50% physical depreciation** per DCAD — meaning the improvement is functionally at or near the end of its economic useful life. With a total DCAD market value of **$161,760**, the critical question is the lot-to-improvement value split: in the 75216 zip code (Oak Cliff / Liberty Heights Addition), comparable lot values in this corridor are running **$40,000–$65,000** for standard residential lots, suggesting the improvement is being carried at roughly **$96,000–$120,000** on the DCAD card — a valuation that almost certainly overstates the functional market value of an 88-year-old, sub-1,000 sq/ft structure with no disclosed exterior finish data and major systems (HVAC, plumbing, electrical, roof) statistically at or past end-of-life. The lot itself in Block 29/4078 of **Liberty Heights Addition** is the durable asset here. Title vested via Warranty Deed recorded **February 19, 1992** — over 33 years ago — under **"SALAZAR ASUSSION EST OF"**, meaning this property transferred into what appears to be an estate holding and has **never been retitled since**. The "EST OF" designation is a critical red flag confirming no probate was completed or the estate was never formally administered, which is why the plaintiff is naming **Asussion Salazar a/k/a Joann Salazar** (the decedent or original owner), plus **Elsias Salazar, Samuel Salazar** (likely heirs, named In Rem), **Lydia S. Cedillo** (heir, unserved, last known 1206 Burlington Blvd., Dallas 75208), **Dolores Garcia** (heir, served, filed pro se General Denial from **1715 Marfa Ave. itself** — confirmed occupant), and **Anna Maria Carpio** (heir, served by attorney mail to Pharr, TX 78577). The payment history — zero homestead exemption, estate','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T10:45:12.998014','2026-07-10T10:45:12.998014','2026-07-10T10:45:12.998014',1,'individual','high','Being Lot 14 in Block 29/4078 of Liberty Heights Addition, an addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded in Volume 92035 Page 1398 of the Deed Records Dallas County, Texas.','{"account_number": "00000302902000000", "market_value": 161760, "land_value": 95000, "improvement_value": 66760, "estimated_annual_taxes": 3601.93, "year_built": 1938, "effective_year_built": 1938, "actual_age": 88, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "POST", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 996, "total_area_sqft": 996, "bedrooms": 2, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 50, "desirability": "AVERAGE", "air_condition": "WINDOW", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": 400, "zoning": "SINGLE FAMILY 7500 SQFT", "lot_frontage_ft": 50, "lot_depth_ft": 175, "lot_area_sqft": 9163.0, "land_unit_price": 95000.0, "leg