'high',NULL,'2024-12-06','JUDGMENT NON-JURY','2026-06-16',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 1147.41, "penaltyInterest": 821.93, "total": 1969.34}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 1270.59, "penaltyInterest": 912.36, "total": 2182.95}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 601.35, "penaltyInterest": 428.71, "total": 1030.06}, {"entity": "Dallas County School Equalization Fund", "taxAmt": 49.31, "penaltyInterest": 34.97, "total": 84.28}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 6248.85, "penaltyInterest": 4479.48, "total": 10728.33}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 3788.9, "penaltyInterest": 2695.64, "total": 6484.54}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Senior Analyst Review**\n**Case:** TX-23-02230 | **Property:** 2915 E. Overton Rd., Dallas, TX 75216\n**Date:** July 2025 | **Classification:** ACTIVE ACQUISITION TARGET — HIGH PRIORITY\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is almost certainly a **land play, not a structure play.** The DCAD distress signal flagging "improvement value near zero" is the critical data point here — the $117,400 market value is being carried almost entirely by the lot itself, which in the Honeycrest Heights submarket of 75216 reflects underlying land demand driven by infill redevelopment pressure along the E. Overton corridor. The legal description references parts of Lots 27-30 and all of Lots 28-29 in Block A/6086, meaning this is a **multi-lot assembled parcel**, which significantly elevates its strategic value for a builder or developer looking for a pad site with enough width and depth to accommodate a new construction duplex or small SFR infill build — both active product types in this zip. With no year-built data populating in DCAD (or a near-zero improvement value returned), the working assumption is that the original structure has either been demolished, condemned, or has deteriorated to the point of zero contributory value. Before any offer is made, a drive-by and Dallas Code Compliance records pull is mandatory to confirm demolition status and whether any active violation or abatement order exists, which could create a hidden cost exposure.\n\nThe ownership chain here tells a layered story. **Idalia Garcia V (a/k/a Idalia Ortega)** acquired the property via warranty deed on **August 1, 2018** (Instrument No. 20180...), and DCAD carries her as 100% owner under the name ORTEGA IDALIA. The absence of a homestead exemption confirms she is **not living at the property** — she is either a non-owner-occupied landlord, has vacated, or abandoned it entirely. The prior ownership chain includes **Billy Mathis Jr., Michele Mathis, Keith Mathis, Dana Mathis, and Gilbert Mathis** — a family ownership cluster, suggesting this was likely an estate or inherited property that Ortega purchased in 2018, possibly at a discount given the family fragmentation. The Mathis defendants are named in rem only, meaning the plaintiffs are foreclosing their residual interest (likely an unperfected lien, vendor''s lien, or deed-of-trust remnant from the 2018','\n',char(10)),NULL,'oos_issued',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T11:58:23.728961','2026-07-10T11:58:23.728961','2026-07-10T11:58:23.728961',1,'individual','high','BEING A PART OF LOT 27 AND ALL OF LOTS 28, 29 AND 30 IN BLOCK A/6086, OF HONEYCREST HEIGHTS, AN ADDITION IN THE CITY OF DALLAS, DALLAS COUNTY, TEXAS, AS SHOWN BY THE WARRANTY DEED RECORDED AS INSTRUMENT NUMBER 201800205738 OF THE DEED RECORDS OF DALLAS COUNTY, TEXAS','{"account_number": "00000509071000000", "market_value": 117400, "land_value": 117400, "improvement_value": 0, "estimated_annual_taxes": 2614.16, "year_built": null, "effective_year_built": null, "actual_age": null, "building_class": "", "construction_type": "", "foundation": "", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": null, "total_area_sqft": null, "bedrooms": null, "bathroom