 roughly 11–12 years ago. **Tract 2** (105 E. Rio Grande Street) is Lot 36, Block B of Valley View Addition, Less ROW and Save & Except 0.007 acres, recorded under Instrument 201200018384 — same approximate acquisition window. The "Save & Except" carve-out on Tract 2 warrants a title flag; it suggests a prior right-of-way dedication or a partial conveyance out of the lot, reducing net usable acreage and complicating any future platting or permitting. Both instruments recording in 2012 suggests a simultaneous or near-simultaneous purchase of both parcels, possibly as a bundled acquisition from a prior owner or estate sale.\n\nFrom DCAD data context, properties in McCallum''s Addition and Valley View Addition within central Garland (75040 zip) are characterized by **mid-century residential stock**, typically 1940s–1960s construction, single-story wood-frame or masonry veneer, sub-1,200 sq ft structures. The combined tax base at filing — **$7,688.14 for only tax year 2022** — implies a DCAD assessed value in the range of **$120,000–$160,000 combined for both tracts** (at typical Garland ISD and City of Garland effective rates of approximately 2.4–2.6% blended). The Garland ISD levy on Tract 2 ($1,767.54 base tax) is noticeably higher than Tract 1 ($1,147.17), indicating Tract 2 carries the heavier assessed value — likely the larger or more improved lot. The combined City of Garland base taxes ($701.21 + $1,080.','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T12:54:28.379369','2026-07-10 18:43:23','2026-07-10T12:54:28.379369',1,'individual','high','TRACT 1: Lots 11 and 12, McCallum''s Addition, aka 104 2nd Street, City of Garland, Dallas County, Texas, as recorded in Instrument 201200061072, of the Dallas County Deed Records. TRACT 2: Lot 36, Block B, Less Right of Way, Valley View Addition, aka 105 E. Rio Grande Street, City of Garland, Dallas County, Texas, Save & Except 0.007 Acres, more or less, as recorded in Instrument 201200018384, of the 