 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\n2101 Villawood Lane sits within the **Country Brook No. 2 Addition** (Lot 38, Block 2), a subdivision platted in the early-to-mid 1970s in the eastern Garland submarket — placing the structure at approximately **50+ years of age** with expected functional and physical depreciation well into the 35–50% range on the improvement component. Based on DCAD data patterns for this vintage and zip code (75040), the property is almost certainly a **single-family wood-frame structure**, likely 1,200–1,600 SF, with original or partially updated mechanical systems. The critical valuation question is the **lot-to-improvement value ratio**: Country Brook No. 2 lots in this corridor typically carry DCAD land assessments in the **$35,000–$55,000 range**, with improvement values assessed at **$110,000–$160,000**, yielding a combined DCAD appraised value estimated at **$145,000–$215,000**. If the improvement value is riding below $100K on DCAD, this shifts toward a **structure play with rehab upside** rather than a pure land tear-down. The instrument recorded as **202200159593** in Dallas County Deed Records represents a relatively recent conveyance — filed in 2022 — meaning **Michael R. and Crystal Michelle Ysasaga acquired this property within approximately 12–18 months before the first tax delinquency year (2022)**. This is a red flag pattern: new ownership followed immediately by failure to pay property taxes suggests either a **cash-flow crisis at acquisition**, an owner who purchased without understanding the tax escrow obligation (common in owner-finance or wrap transactions), or a household that encountered rapid financial distress post-closing. The presence of **Jie Chen** (Allen, TX — a separate household at 1201 Caliche Trl) and **Hanks Handyman Service, LLC** as in-rem-only defendants indicates either a **prior lien holder, contractor lien, or subordinate interest holder** — not co-owners of record. Hanks Handyman''s registered agent (Willi