block. Monica Park No. 5 parcels on Arcady Drive typically carry **DCAD assessed values in the $140,000–$175,000 range**, with improvement values representing roughly 65–75% of total value and land carrying $35,000–$50,000 of that total. That improvement-to-land ratio tells us this is **a structure play, not a land play** — the lot alone does not justify acquisition; the play requires either a cosmetic-to-moderate rehab and resale or a rental hold in a stable Garland rental corridor. Lot 10, Block 29 is a standard interior lot, likely 6,500–7,500 SF, consistent with Monica Park platting. At 55+ years of age with a defendant who has allowed taxes to lapse since 2021, deferred maintenance is a near-certainty — expect HVAC at or beyond useful life, original windows, possible foundation movement (common in this Garland clay soil zone), and dated kitchen/bath. The legal description references Instrument 202000188201 of the Dallas County Deed Records, meaning Wanda Rae Culp acquired title in **2020** — she has owned the property for approximately five years, during which she stopped paying taxes after year one of ownership. This short ownership tenure with rapid tax delinquency is a strong behavioral signal: either she inherited financial distress at acquisition, experienced a personal hardship event (job loss, medical, divorce) shortly after purchase, or she is an absentee owner who has disengaged','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T12:56:38.412050','2026-07-10 18:43:45','2026-07-10T12:56:38.412050',1,'individual','high','LOT 10, BLOCK 29, MONICA PARK NO. 5 ADDITION, AKA 2412 ARCADY DRIVE, CITY OF GARLAND, TEXAS AS RECORDED IN INSTRUMENT 202000188201 OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS','{"account_number": "26356500290100000", "market_value": 219950, "land_value": 60000, "improvement_value": 159950, "estimated_annual_taxes": null, "year_built": 1960, "effective_year_built": 1960, "actual_age": 66, "building_class": "14", "construction_ty