INSERT INTO cases VALUES(98,'TX-23-02246','101st District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2023-12-19','CLOSED','TAX DELINQUENCY','GUZMAN, ENRIQUE','[{"name": "Enrique Guzman", "address": "719 Dowdy Ferry Rd., Dallas, TX 75217", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Private Process Server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Served 01/22/2024; Executed citation returned 02/26/2024"}, {"name": "Juanita Guzman", "address": "719 Dowdy Ferry Rd., Dallas, TX 75217", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Private Process Server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Served 01/22/2024; Executed citation returned 02/26/2024; Filed Original Answer - General Denial 01/24/2024"}]','1314 Narcissus Ln., Mesquite, TX 75149-6125',NULL,'38103500030100000','LGBS (Linebarger)','LANE, BRANDON EDWARD',16803.0,2020,'[2020, 2021, 2022]',2,0,0,'[]',0,0,0,'','low',NULL,'2024-09-10','DEFAULT JUDGMENT',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 894.04, "penaltyInterest": 554.18, "total": 1448.22}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 986.63, "penaltyInterest": 612.79, "total": 1599.42}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 474.13, "penaltyInterest": 293.28, "total": 767.41}, {"entity": "Dallas County School Equalization Fund", "taxAmt": 39.18, "penaltyInterest": 24.12, "total": 63.3}, {"entity": "Mesquite Independent School District", "taxAmt": 5269.3, "penaltyInterest": 3272.26, "total": 8541.56}, {"entity": "City of Mesquite", "taxAmt": 2707.5, "penaltyInterest": 1675.59, "total": 4383.09}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Tax Foreclosure Analysis**\n\n---\n\n**CASE:** TX-23-02246 | **PROPERTY:** 1314 Narcissus Ln., Mesquite, TX 75149-6125\n**PREPARED FOR:** Acquisitions Team | **COURT:** 101st District Court — Judge Carl Ginsberg\n**STATUS:** ⚠️ DEFAULT JUDGMENT ENTERED 09/10/2024 — POST-JUDGMENT PHASE ACTIVE\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is fundamentally a **land play with a functional-but-declining structure component.** The subject is a 975 sq ft single-family residence built in **1960 — now 65 years old** — carrying a **50% depreciation factor per DCAD**, which signals the structure is assessed as being at or near the midpoint of its economic useful life. At 975 sq ft on a residential lot in Highland Hills Addition (Lot 10, Block C), the improvement contributes diminishing value relative to the land. DCAD''s market value sits at **$179,170**, but given the age, size, and depreciation load, the improvement-to-land value split is almost certainly skewed toward the land — in Mesquite''s 75149 zip code, comparable land values for similarly platted residential lots run **$40,000–$65,000 bare**, suggesting the structure itself is contributing perhaps **$110,000–$130,000** to the assessed value on paper, but a realistic investor ARV after cosmetic to moderate rehab would need verification via comp pull. The exterior condition is **unreported in DCAD**, which is itself a red flag — it may indicate the structure has not been re-inspected recently or the appraiser defaulted to cost-approach values without a physical review. The ownership chain tells a critical story: **RIDGEVIEW HOLDINGS LP** held and paid taxes through **2009**; prior to that, **VELLA CLARK** paid through **2003**, and **CLARK LEN** through **1999**. The current legal owner, **Enrique Guzman** (with co-defendant **Juanita Guzman**), acquired via General Warranty Deed recorded as **Instrument No. 20100008385** — meaning they purchased from Ridgeview Holdings LP around **2010** and have not paid a single year of property taxes in what the DCAD distress flag identifies as **17 years of non-payment** (delinquency confirmed from 2020 forward in the suit, but the 17-year','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T13:01:41.946112','2026-07-10T13:01:41.946112','2026-07-10T13:01:41.946112',1,'individual','high','Lot 10, Block C, of Highland Hills Addition, an Ad