INSERT INTO cases VALUES(100,'TX-23-02233','101st District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2023-12-18','CLOSED','TAX DELINQUENCY','DIANA GARCIA A/K/A DIANA SANCHEZ A/K/A DIANA PEREZ','[{"name": "DIANA GARCIA A/K/A DIANA SANCHEZ A/K/A DIANA PEREZ", "address": "2805 W WALNUT ST, GARLAND, TX 75042", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Constable", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Executed citation returned 02/05/2024"}, {"name": "U.S. BANK TRUST NATIONAL ASSOCIATION AS TRUSTEE OF THE BKPL LODGE SERIES I TRUST, BY SERVING REGISTERED AGENT, CT CORPORATION SYSTEM BY SERVING ITS OFFICER OR AGENT AUTHORIZED TO ACCEPT SERVICE", "address": "1999 BRYAN ST., SUITE 900, DALLAS, TX 75201", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Attorney/Mail", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Executed citation returned 02/14/2024; In Rem Only"}]','2805 W Walnut St, Garland, TX 75042',NULL,'26665500090080000','Perdue Brandon Fielder Collins & Mott','LINDA D. REECE',7599.8299999999998632,2020,'[2020, 2022]',2,0,0,'[]',0,0,0,'Initial citation to U.S. Bank required re-service; second citation issued 01/12/2024','medium',NULL,'2024-07-16','NON-SUIT/DISMISSAL BY PLAINTIFF / PETITIONER',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "GARLAND INDEPENDENT SCHOOL DISTRICT", "taxAmt": 2121.64, "penaltyInterest": 1035.36, "total": 3157.0}, {"entity": "CITY OF GARLAND", "taxAmt": 2514.82, "penaltyInterest": 1578.01, "total": 4092.83}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Internal Use Only**\n**Case:** TX-23-02233 | 101st District Court (Judge Ginsberg)\n**Subject Property:** 2805 W Walnut St, Garland, TX 75042\n**Prepared By:** Acquisitions Analysis Desk\n**Date:** June 2025\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe subject is a single-family residential structure on Lot 8, Block 9 of the Western Heights Addition in Garland — a mid-century subdivision platted in the early 1950s, meaning this structure is likely **70+ years old** and carrying substantial physical depreciation. Western Heights sits west of Downtown Garland, north of Walnut Street''s commercial corridor, and represents one of the older working-class residential pockets in the city. DCAD records for this area typically show improvement-to-land value ratios that are **compressed** — structures in this vintage range often carry improvement values of $80,000–$110,000 against land values of $35,000–$55,000, suggesting this is **primarily a structure play** rather than a land-only acquisition, though the land component is not negligible given Garland''s infill pressure. At 70+ years, a wood-frame structure of this era without documented renovation will carry DCAD-applied depreciation of **40–60%** off replacement cost, and roof, HVAC, plumbing, and foundation issues should be assumed until inspected. The defendant — **Diana Garcia a/k/a Diana Sanchez a/k/a Diana Perez** — presents three name variants, a pattern consistent with multiple marriages, name changes, or identity documentation inconsistencies. This is operationally significant for skip tracing and title work. The delinquency years of **2020 and 2022** (notably not consecutive, with 2021 apparently current) suggest an owner making selective payments under financial stress rather than complete abandonment — she paid 2021 taxes but let 2020 and 2022 lapse, which indicates awareness of the tax obligation and periodic access to funds, not a vacant-and-walked-away scenario. The presence of **U.S. Bank Trust National Association as Trustee of the BKPL Lodge Series I Trust** as an in-rem-only defendant confirms an **active mortgage lien** on the property. BKPL Lodge Series I is a non-performing loan (NPL) trust vehicle — this is not a traditional bank servicer. This means the mortgage is almost certainly delinquent or in default, adding a **second layer of financial distress**','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T13:03:59.764869','2026-07-10 18:44:22','2026-07-10T13:03:59.7648