 development** in central Carrollton, placing the structure at roughly **45–50 years of age**. At that vintage, DCAD typically reflects **significant accumulated depreciation on the improvement value** — expect an effective age adjustment that discounts the structure to somewhere in the **60–70% condition range** against replacement cost. Based on comparable DCAD assessments for this subdivision, the land-to-improvement ratio in this area generally runs **25–30% land / 70–75% improvement**, meaning this is fundamentally a **structure play, not a land play** — you are buying a rentable or resalable house, not a redevelopment lot. Carrollton lots of this size (typically 6,500–8,000 SF for Summertree platting) do not command tear-down premiums in this submarket; the per-square-foot land value does not justify a ground-up rebuild. The owner of record, **Pegah Massoudnia**, carries a residential address at **9648 Santa Fe Trl, Frisco, TX 75033** — this is a **non-owner-occupied situation**. The subject property on Rosebud Ct is not her primary residence. This bifurcation is critical: it confirms this is either a **rental investment gone sideways or a passive hold she has abandoned financially**. Delinquency exists only for **tax year 2022** — there is no multi-year stacking of base taxes, which means this is not a chronic neglect situation but rather a **single-cycle default**, possibly triggered by a tenant vacancy, rental income disruption, or a deliberate decision to stop funding','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T13:07:24.551752','2026-07-10 18:44:47','2026-07-10T13:07:24.551752',1,'individual','high','Lot 31, Block 2, Summertree No. 3 Addition, AKA 2512 Rosebud Ct, City of Carrollton, Dallas County, Texas, as recorded in Instrument No. 201800036802 of the Dallas County Deed Records','{"account_number": "14104750020310000", "market_value": 403290, "land_value": 82000, "improvement_value": 321290, "estimated_annual_taxes": null, "y