: 10215.34}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n## PC Peak Development | Tax Foreclosure Case Analysis\n**Case:** TX-23-02227 | **Property:** 3715 Dunbar St., Dallas, TX 75215\n**Prepared by:** Senior Acquisition Analyst | **Date:** June 2025\n**Priority Rating:** 🔴 HIGH | **Distress Score:** 5/5\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is a **land play with a distressed structure complication.** The DCAD profile tells a clear story: a 1,064 sq ft wood-frame residence built in 1925, now 101 years old, carrying a 50% depreciation flag — meaning DCAD''s own assessors have marked the structure as being at or near the end of its functional economic life. At a $136,480 market value with meaningful improvement value still on the books, the land component in the 75215 zip corridor is doing the heavy lifting here. Wheatley Place Addition (Lot 4, Block 3/1962) sits in a South Dallas pocket that has seen incremental infill pressure, making the underlying dirt more interesting than anything sitting on it. A 1,064 sq ft century-old structure with 50% depreciation and unknown exterior condition (no cladding data returned from DCAD pull) is functionally a tear-down candidate or an extreme rehab — neither is cheap. **Do not underwrite this as a rental stabilization play.** Major systems — HVAC, electrical, plumbing, roof — on a 1925 structure are all presumptively at end of life absent documented renovation evidence, and none exists in the deed or permit record.\n\nThe ownership chain is revealing. **Powell Albert** paid taxes in 2002, **Powell Albert E** in 2003, and then **Henderson Alfredia** shows a payment in 2004 — suggesting a family transfer or sale occurred right at the 2003/2004 boundary. The deed of record (Instrument No. 202200096789, filed 12/30/2022) confirms Henderson acquired the property via General Warranty Deed just 29 months ago, meaning she is a relatively recent titleholder, not a multi-decade legacy owner. Critically, she holds a **homestead exemption**, confirming owner-occupancy at time of filing. The delinquency string, however, runs from **2004 through 2022** (skipping only 2015), meaning the tax debt predates her 2022 acquisition — she either inherited the debt through the purchase or acquired a property already drowning in back taxes, possibly without full disclosure or','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T13:11:02.594390','2026-07-10T13:11:02.594390','2026-07-10T13:11:02.594390',1,'individual','high','LOT 4, BLOCK 3/1962, OF WHEATLEY PLACE ADDITION, AN ADDITION IN THE CITY OF DALLAS, DALLAS COUNTY, TEXAS, AS SHOWN BY THE GENERAL WARRANTY DEED RECORDED AS INSTRUMENT NUMBER 202200096789 OF THE DEED RECORDS OF DALLAS COUNTY, TEXAS','{"account_number": "00000189235000000", "market_value": 136480, "land_value": 50000, "improvement_value": 86480, "estimated_annual_taxes": 49.05, "year_built": 1925, "effective_year_built": 1925, "actual_age": 101, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "POST", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 1064, "total_area_sqft": 1064, "bedrooms": 2, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 50, "desirability": "AVERAGE", "air_condition": "NONE", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "PLANNED DEVELOPMENT DISTRICT", "lot_frontage_ft": 50, "lot_depth_ft": 110, "lot_area_sqft": 0.0, "land_unit_price": 50000.0, "legal_description": "1: WHEATLEY PLACE 2: BLK 3/1962 LOT 4 3: 4: INT202200326051 DD12282022 CO-DC 5: 1962 003 00400 1001962 003 Deed Transfer Date: 12/30/2022", "owners": [{"name": "HENDERSON ALFREDIA", "pct": 100}], "deed_transfer_date": "12/30/2022", "exemptions": "City\tSchool\tCounty\tCollege\tHospital\tSpecial District", "no_homestead": false, "tax_rates": [{"entity": "DALLAS\tDALLAS ISD\tDALLAS COUNTY\tDALLAS COLLEGE\tPARKLAND HOSPITAL\tUNASSIGNED\nHOMESTEAD EXEMPTION", "estimated_tax": 27296.0}], "current_tax_balance": 43065.54, "current_levy