3650.7, "penaltyInterest": 2672.96, "total": 6323.66}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Tax Foreclosure Division**\n**Case No. TX-23-02219 | 1510–1514 Garza Ave., Dallas, TX 75216**\n**Prepared By:** Senior Acquisition Analyst\n**Date:** June 2025\n**Priority Rating:** 🔴 HIGH — POST-JUDGMENT, PRE-SALE\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is a **dual-lot play** involving two adjacent parcels — Lot 13 (1514 Garza) and Lot 14 (1510 Garza) — both recorded under the same Warranty Deed instrument (No. 200600064038), acquired simultaneously on **February 21, 2006**, by Cristoval Guerrero and Maria E. Juarez as **50/50 co-owners**. The structure sitting on the combined footprint is a **1,290 sq ft residential structure built in 1931**, placing it at **95 years of age** with DCAD-assessed depreciation of **50%** — meaning the taxing authority itself has marked the improvements as near the end of their functional economic life. At a market value of **$287,390** across both tracts combined, the land component is doing the heavy lifting here. A 1,290 sq ft structure with 50% depreciation in the 75216 zip code is not a rehab play under conventional lending — it is either a teardown or a deep-discount cash renovation. The **absence of any homestead exemption** is a critical signal: neither Guerrero nor Juarez has claimed this as a primary residence, strongly suggesting **absentee ownership** — possibly rentals, long-term neglect, or family property that has drifted out of active management. The 2006 acquisition likely represents a purchase near the height of pre-crash values in this Dallas South corridor, and the delinquency pattern — running **continuously from 2016 through 2022** (seven consecutive years) — tells the story of owners who either lost financial capacity or lost interest in the asset entirely. A single payment appearing in **2024** (per DCAD payment history) is notable but does not reflect engagement with the lawsuit; it may represent a partial payment or a single-year catch-up that did not address the cumulative arrearage. The **lot-to-improvement value ratio** strongly favors land: at 50% depreciation on a 95-year-old structure, improvement value is likely assessed in the **$60,000–$85,000 range**, with raw land value carrying **$200,000+**','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T13:17:23.178115','2026-07-10T13:17:23.178115','2026-07-10T13:17:23.178115',1,'individual','high','Tract 1: Lot 13, in Block 11/4311 of Bellview, an Addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded as Instrument Number 200600064038 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas. Tract 2: Lot 14, Block 11/4311, of Bellview, an Addition in the City of Dallas, Dallas County, Texas, as shown by the Warranty Deed recorded as Instrument Number 200600064038 of the Deed Records of Dallas County, Texas.','{"account_number": "00000315871000000, 00000315874000000", "market_value": 287390, "land_value": 160000, "improvement_value": 127390, "estimated_annual_taxes": 6399.34, "year_built": 1931, "effective_year_built": 1931, "actual_age": 95, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "BLOCK", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 1290, "total_area_sqft": 1290, "bedrooms": 2, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 50, "desirability": "AVERAGE", "air_condition": "WINDOW", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "SINGLE FAMILY 7500 SQFT", "lot_frontage_ft": 50, "lot_depth_ft": 236, "lot_area_sqft": 23844.0, "land_unit_price": 80000.0, "legal_description": "1: BELLEVUE 2: BLK 11/4311 LOT 13 3: 4: INT200600064038 DD02172006 CO-DC 5: 4311 011 01300 2004311 011 Deed Transfer Date: 2/21/2006", "owners": [{"name": "GUERRERO CRISTOVAL &", "pct": 50}, {"name": "JUANREZ MARIA E", "pct": 50}], "deed_transfer_date": "2/21/2006", "exemptions": "None", "no_homestead": true,