INSERT INTO cases VALUES(113,'TX-24-00094','191st District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2024-01-24','CLOSED','TAX DELINQUENCY','WALTER G. ORDONEZ AKA WALTER C. ORDONEZ','[{"name": "WALTER G. ORDONEZ AKA WALTER C. ORDONEZ", "address": "1605 Dove Drive, Garland, TX 75040", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Constable", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Executed citation 04/22/2024"}, {"name": "MARIA E. FARIAS-SANCHEZ", "address": "1605 Dove Drive, Garland, TX 75040", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Constable", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Executed citation 04/22/2024"}, {"name": "DAWN MARIE WARREN", "address": "4713 Lloyd Court, Flower Mound, TX 75028", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Attorney/Mail", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Executed citation 04/23/2024; IN REM ONLY"}]','1605 Dove Drive, Garland, TX 75040',NULL,'26462500170020000','Perdue Brandon Fielder Collins & Mott','REECE, LINDA D.',5917.8199999999998581,2022,'[2022]',3,0,0,'[]',0,1,0,'Initial citations returned unexecuted 04/05/2024 for all three defendants; re-issued 04/06/2024 and subsequently served','medium',NULL,'2025-01-13','NON-SUIT/DISMISSAL BY PLAINTIFF / PETITIONER',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "GARLAND INDEPENDENT SCHOOL DISTRICT", "taxAmt": 2621.36, "penaltyInterest": 1279.23, "total": 3900.59}, {"entity": "CITY OF GARLAND", "taxAmt": 1120.45, "penaltyInterest": 546.78, "total": 1667.23}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Senior Acquisitions Desk**\n**Case:** TX-24-00094 | **Property:** 1605 Dove Drive, Garland, TX 75040\n**Analyst Date:** Current | **Priority Classification:** MONITOR / LOW-URGENCY OPPORTUNISTIC\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe subject property is a 1,436 SF single-family residence built in 1977, now 49 years old, situated on Lot 2, Block 17 of the Quail Creek No. 4 Addition in Garland. DCAD carries a market value of **$260,960**, but the 45% depreciation flag is critical — at nearly five decades old with no recorded exterior cladding data populating in DCAD, this structure likely presents deferred maintenance consistent with an absentee-owned rental: think original HVAC equipment, aging roof (potentially third or fourth generation needed), possibly original plumbing and electrical panel. The improvement-to-land ratio at this valuation in Quail Creek suggests this is **primarily a structure play, not a land play** — the lot itself in this submarket is not commanding premium teardown economics, so value is contingent on the livability and rehab cost of the existing 1,436 SF frame. The absence of a homestead exemption is the loudest signal in this file: neither Walter C. Ordonez nor Maria E. Farias-Sanchez is claiming this as a primary residence, confirming absentee/investor ownership or a landlord situation where tenants may currently occupy. Title transferred **August 26, 2013** per the deed recorded at Instrument 201300270189 — the co-owners have held this asset for roughly 12 years, suggesting it was likely acquired as a rental investment. The 50/50 ownership split between Farias-Sanchez and Ordonez, combined with the third defendant **Dawn Marie Warren** (served in rem only at a Flower Mound address), indicates a possible prior lienholder, subordinate interest holder, or previous owner with a recorded instrument — her in-rem-only designation means the taxing units are clearing her interest without asserting personal liability, which is standard for junior lienholders or former title holders with residual recorded claims. No prior related suits exist in the file, meaning this is the first time these owners have been dragged into tax court on this property.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nThe filing amount at suit inception on **January 24, 2024** was **$5,917.82**, covering delinqu','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T14:58:35.981545','2026-07-10T14:58:35.981545','2026-07-10T14:58:35.98