h Rowlett''s sustained demand corridor along the Lake Ray Hubbard suburban ring. The improvement value is the dominant value driver here; the land component in Westwood Estates No. 6 is contributory but secondary. The 35% depreciation flag is meaningful — at 34 years with no exterior material documented in DCAD, this property likely presents deferred maintenance: aging HVAC, original roof approaching or past end-of-life, possible foundation settling common to early-1990s Dallas-area slab construction, and cosmetic deterioration. Budget conservatively **$35,000–$55,000** in renovation exposure before this asset is retail-ready or rental-stabilized. The ownership trail tells the critical story: **Dorothy Lee Dixon** was the original occupant-owner, appearing on payment records through 2019–2020. **Dorothy Lee Estate of** appears on 2021–2022 payments, confirming Dorothy died sometime in 2020–2021. **Robert Douglas Dixon** — almost certainly a son or close heir — absorbed the account and made a 2022 payment but has since gone delinquent. The **deed transfer dated 3/12/2025** is the most operationally significant data point in this file: title moved during active litigation, suggesting either a probate distribution, a quitclaim among heirs, or an attempt to restructure ownership ahead of judgment. Robert Douglas Dixon''s known address of **802 Broadway Commons, Garland, TX 75043** indicates he is not living at the subject property — the homestead exemption may be legacy/grandfathered from Dorothy''s occupancy and warrants verification with DCAD for current validity.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nThe tax filing amount','\n',char(10)),NULL,'oos_issued',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T14:59:55.950710','2026-07-10T14:59:55.950710','2026-07-10T14:59:55.950710',1,'estate','high','LOT 15, BLOCK 2, WESTWOOD ESTATES NO. 6 ADDITION, AKA 3005 COTTONWOOD COURT, CITY OF ROWLETT, TEXAS AS RECORDED IN VOLUME 93166, PAGE 4400 OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS','{"account_numbe