INSERT INTO cases VALUES(117,'TX-24-00090','298th District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2024-01-23','CLOSED','TAX DELINQUENCY','BAHENA, PABLO MARGARITO','[{"name": "PABLO MARGARITO BAHENA", "address": "5167 CR 2507, Caddo Mills, TX 75135", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Attorney/Mail", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Initially unserved; re-cited 06/06/2024; executed citation returned 07/17/2024"}, {"name": "LUCIA BAHENA", "address": "5167 CR 2507, Caddo Mills, TX 75135", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Rule 106 Substitute Service", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Rule 106 order signed 04/05/2024; executed citation returned 04/17/2024"}]','704 Hiland Street, Garland, TX',NULL,'26264500050080000','Perdue Brandon Fielder Collins & Mott','REECE, LINDA D.',9233.7600000000001898,2020,'[2020, 2021, 2022]',2,0,1,'[]',0,0,0,'Pablo Margarito Bahena initially unserved twice before successful service on third citation; Lucia Bahena required Rule 106 substitute service order before execution','medium',NULL,'2024-10-17','DEFAULT JUDGMENT',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "GARLAND INDEPENDENT SCHOOL DISTRICT", "taxAmt": 5643.46, "penaltyInterest": 3240.3, "total": 8883.76}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n## PC Peak Development | Tax Foreclosure Analysis\n**Case:** TX-24-00090 | **Property:** 704 Hiland Street, Garland, TX 75040\n**Prepared By:** Senior Acquisitions Analyst | **Date:** June 2025\n**Priority:** ⚠️ MONITOR / REASSESS — Post-Judgment, Taxes Paid, Live Equity Play\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\n704 Hiland Street is a 1,220 sq ft single-family structure built in **1949** and currently carrying **50% physical depreciation** per DCAD — placing it squarely at or near the end of its conventional economic life by appraisal standards. At 77 years old with a depreciated structure on a Garland residential lot, this case demands immediate classification: **this is primarily a land and assemblage play, not a structure play.** DCAD''s $240,030 market value is driven by the underlying lot value and Garland''s absorbed suburban land pricing, not the aged wood-frame structure sitting on it. The improvement-to-land value ratio almost certainly skews toward land dominance here — a 1,220 sq ft 1949 structure at 50% depreciation likely carries an improvement value in the $60,000–$80,000 range at best, suggesting **land accounts for approximately $160,000–$180,000 of the $240,030 total assessed value**. Any renovation underwrite needs to account for the real possibility that the structure requires a full gut or tear-down, not a cosmetic flip. Prior payment history is instructive: **Colonial Savings FA paid in 2011 and Colonial Savings paid in 1998**, indicating a mortgage instrument was active on this property for at least a 13-year window. **Lucia Bahena paid in 2025**, confirming the delinquency has now been cured and the tax lien is satisfied — but also confirming active owner occupancy with a homestead exemption in place. Pablo Margarito Bahena and Lucia Bahena are co-owners at the same address, consistent with a married couple owner-occupant scenario at the subject property itself. The homestead exemption is live, meaning this is their primary residence, which materially affects both legal leverage and seller motivation psychology. No prior related suits exist, suggesting this is a first-time financial distress event for these owners — not a chronic tax defaulter pattern.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nAt filing on **January 23, 2024**, the total certified debt was **','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T15:03:50.270769','2026-07-10T15:03:50.270769','2026-07-10T15:03:50.270769',1,'individual','high','LOT 8, BLOCK E, HILAND ADDITION, AKA 704 HILAND STREET, CITY OF GARLAND, TEXAS AS RECORDED IN VOLUME 87013, PAGE 5189 OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS','{"account_number": "26264500050080000", "market_value": 240030, "land_value": 65