INSERT INTO cases VALUES(126,'TX-24-00074','95th District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2024-01-19','CLOSED','TAX DELINQUENCY','Robert Bryan Peck','[{"name": "Robert Bryan Peck", "address": "5737 Wilford Drive, McKinney, TX 75070", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "Private Process Server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Citation returned unexecuted 03/25/2024"}]','15911 Archwood Ln., Dallas, TX 75248-3534',NULL,'00000799888380000','LGBS (Linebarger)','ATKINS, ASHLY STEELE',13435.040000000000315,2021,'[2021, 2022]',1,0,0,'[]',0,0,0,'Citation issued 02/02/2024 returned unexecuted 03/25/2024; defendant never served prior to dismissal','medium',NULL,'2024-09-27','NON-SUIT/DISMISSAL BY PLAINTIFF / PETITIONER',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 749.08, "penaltyInterest": 414.69, "total": 1163.77}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 822.99, "penaltyInterest": 456.59, "total": 1279.58}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 401.77, "penaltyInterest": 222.69, "total": 624.46}, {"entity": "Dallas County School Equalization Fund", "taxAmt": 33.68, "penaltyInterest": 18.59, "total": 52.27}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 4085.98, "penaltyInterest": 2263.04, "total": 6349.02}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 2553.25, "penaltyInterest": 1412.69, "total": 3965.94}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Dallas Acquisitions Desk**\n**Case:** TX-24-00074 | **Property:** 15911 Archwood Ln., Dallas, TX 75248-3534\n**Prepared:** 2025 | **Analyst:** Senior Acquisitions\n**Priority:** MONITOR / LOW URGENCY\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is a **condominium unit play, not a land play.** The subject is Unit 1027 of Prestonwood Country Club Condominiums, Building B — a 1,497 sq ft unit built in 1968, now carrying **45% depreciation** against a DCAD market value of $262,300. At 58 years of age, the structure has meaningful deferred maintenance exposure typical of late-1960s Dallas condo construction: original mechanical systems likely on second or third replacement cycles, potential slab plumbing issues common to that era, and shared-element liability baked into the .57373% common interest ownership. The depreciation flag is the single meaningful distress signal here — at 45%, DCAD is essentially telling us this unit''s improvement value is absorbing significant wear, though the Prestonwood Country Club submarket provides locational support that keeps the headline number at $262K. Peck acquired via General Warranty Deed recorded as Instrument No. 201900308952 in November 2019 — he paid Providence Title at closing, consistent with a clean retail purchase. The payment history chain (BAC Tax Services 2013 → Providence Title 2019 → Peck 2020 → Resolution Finance LLC 2024 → Peck 2025) is highly revealing: **Resolution Finance LLC''s 2024 payment is the critical data point.** This is a third-party tax lender — Peck could not or did not pay his 2021–2022 delinquency directly, so he borrowed against the property to cure it. He then made the 2025 payment himself. The homestead exemption is active and confirmed, meaning Peck lives here. This is an **owner-occupied, stabilized individual who had a two-year liquidity event (2021–2022), resolved it through tax lending, and has since normalized payments.** Distress score of 1 is accurate.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nThe numbers here tell a story of **resolved distress, not active distress.** At filing on January 19, 2024, Linebarger/LGBS entered suit with a total due of **$13,435.04**','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T15:16:23.142120','2026-07-10T15:16:23.142120','2026-07-10T15:16:23.142120',1,'individual','high','Being Unit 1027, of the Prestonwood Country Club Condominiums, Building B, located on Block A/8219, together with a .57373 interest in the common elements thereon. A condominium regime in the City of Dall