te:** May 2025\n**Priority Rating:** 🔴 CRITICAL — Immediate Action Required\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe subject property is a 1,951-vintage, 1,300 sq/ft single-family residence situated on Lot 14, Block 6/6323 of Oak Hill Park Annex in Dallas 75217. DCAD assigns a **market value of $246,940**, but the 50% structural depreciation flag is the headline concern here — at 74 years old with half its economic life consumed, the improvement itself is approaching functional obsolescence. The critical valuation question is the land-to-improvement split: in the 75217 zip code, lot values in Oak Hill Park Annex are increasingly relevant as infill pressure builds along the southeast Dallas corridor. Until we pull the DCAD land vs. improvement breakdown explicitly, we treat this as a **hybrid play leaning land** — the structure adds some rental utility near-term but is unlikely to support a full renovation underwrite without significant capital. Deed transfer records via Instrument No. 201500329318 confirm **Juan Manuel Martinez acquired the property on 12/15/2015**, roughly a decade ago. Prior payment history is telling: **Nicandra Sias paid taxes through 2011**, and **Willie Mae Speight paid through 2007**, suggesting the property cycled through at least two prior owners before Martinez. What''s damning is the payment gap — **no tax payment has been recorded in approximately 14 years**, meaning neither Sias nor Martinez has carried current tax obligations in over a decade. Martinez took title into a distressed payment posture and never corrected it. The homestead exemption is active, confirming owner-occupancy — Martinez and co-defendant **Nora Elia Carrizales** (likely a spouse or partner sharing the same address of record) are living in the home or were recently. This is not an absentee landlord situation. Expect emotional attachment, possible language barriers, and resistance to unsolicited contact — but also genuine financial distress that creates real motivation to transact.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nAt filing on **January 19, 2024**, Linebarger Goggan (LGBS) recorded a total delinquency of **$12,766.65**, covering tax years **2021','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T15:17:48.152814','2026-07-10T15:17:48.152814','2026-07-10T15:17:48.152814',1,'individual','high','BEING LOT FOURTEEN (14), IN BLOCK 6/6323, OF OAK HILL PARK ANNEX IN THE CITY OF DALLAS, DALLAS COUNTY, TEXAS, AS SHOWN BY THE GENERAL WARRANTY DEED RECORDED AS INSTRUMENT NUMBER 201500329318 OF THE DEED RECORDS OF DALLAS COUNTY, TEXAS','{"account_number": "00000565474000000", "market_value": 246940, "land_value": 70000, "improvement_value": 176940, "estimated_annual_taxes": 3252.96, "year_built": 1951, "effective_year_built": 1951, "actual_age": 75, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "PIER AND BEAM", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 1300, "total_area_sqft": 1300, "bedrooms": 3, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 50, "desirability": "AVERAGE", "air_condition": "CENTRAL FULL", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": 276, "zoning": "SINGLE FAMILY 7500 SQFT", "lot_frontage_ft": 75, "lot_depth_ft": 126, "lot_area_sqft": 10043.0, "land_unit_price": 70000.0, "legal_description": "1: OAK HILL PARK ANNEX 2: BLK 6/6323 LT 14 3: 4: INT201500329318 DD11142015 CO-DC 5: 6323 006 01400 3006323 006 Deed Transfer Date: 12/15/2015", "owners": [{"name": "MARTINEZ JUAN MANUEL &", "pct": 100}], "deed_transfer_date": "12/15/2015", "exemptions": "City\tSchool\tCounty\tCollege\tHospital\tSpecial District", "no_homestead": false, "tax_rates": [{"entity": "DALLAS\tDALLAS ISD\tDALLAS COUNTY\tDALLAS COLLEGE\tPARKLAND HOSPITAL\tUNASSIGNED\nHOMESTEAD EXEMPTION", "estimated_tax": 49388.0}], "current_tax_balance": 22339.74, "current_levy": 5352.56, "prior_year_due": 22339.74, "payment_history": [{"date": "2012-02-22", "amount": 1438.85, "tax_year": "2011