family residence built in 1990 — now 36 years old — sitting on a lot within the Lake Bend Estates Phase 2 subdivision in Rowlett. At a $360,000 market value with 35% depreciation flagged on the structure, the improvement itself is carrying meaningful physical wear. That depreciation figure suggests deferred maintenance, aging mechanicals, and likely cosmetic deterioration consistent with a home that has passed through **four distinct ownership/payment periods in four consecutive years** — Barrett Land (2022), Laura Davidson (2023), Leslie J. Davidson (2024), and most recently Truly Title Inc. facilitating a deed transfer on **February 3, 2025** to current owners **Joe Myungjin & Kambry (100% interest)**. That chain tells a specific story: this property was almost certainly held by the Davidson family — likely Barrett Land as a holding entity tied to the same family cluster given the shared surnames and the Leslie Land a/k/a Leslie Davidson alias on file — and cycled through relatives or related entities before being sold outright in early 2025. The fact that Truly Title processed the close confirms a **legitimate arm''s-length or near-arm''s-length sale** occurred, with the new owners now holding a homestead exemption, indicating they moved in as a primary residence. The lot-to-improvement value ratio at 35% structural depreciation on a $360K valuation means approximately **$234,000 is attributable to the structure and $126,000+ to land**, consistent with Rowlett''s Lake Bend corridor where dirt alone has appreciated significantly post-2020. Prior payment history was erratic but ultimately resolved — each year a different party cured the delinquency, which speaks to a fragmented, multi-party ownership structure that created the tax delinquency in the first place rather than financial inability to pay.\n\n---\n\n## ¶2 — FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nThe live tax balance on DCAD shows **$0.00**, and the payment history confirms this was resolved — Truly Title Inc. paid in 2025, almost certainly at or just before the February 3, 2025 ','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T15:20:37.745498','2026-07-10T15:20:37.745498','2026-07-10T15:20:37.745498',1,'individual','high','LOT 22, BLOCK 3, LAKE BEND ESTATES PHASE 2 ADDITION, AKA 8213 BRENTWOOD STREET, CITY OF ROWLETT, TEXAS AS RECORDED IN INSTRUMENT 202000321085 OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS','{"account_number": "44009010030220000", "market_value": 360000, "land_value": 80000, "improvement_value": 280000, "estimated_annual_taxes": 7163.11, "year_built": 1990, "effective_year_built": 1990, "actual_age": 36, "building_class": "16", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "SLAB", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 2802, "total_area_sqft": 2802, "bedrooms": 4, "bathrooms": "", "stories": "", "depreciation_pct": 35, "desirability": "GOOD", "air_condition": "CENTRAL FULL", "heating": "", "garage_sqft": null, "zoning": "SINGLE FAMILY DWELLING R-2", "lot_frontage_ft": 79, "lot_depth_ft": 120, "lot_area_sqft": 9761.0, "land_unit_price": 80000.0, "legal_description": "1: LAKE BEND ESTATES PH 2 2: BLK 3 LOT 22 3: 4: INT202600022426 DD02022026 CO-DC 5: 0090100302200 1CW00901003 Deed Transfer Date: 2/3/2025", "owners": [{"name": "JOE MYUNGJIN & KAMBRY", "pct": 100}], "deed_transfer_date": "2/3/2025", "exemptions": "City\tSchool\tCounty\tCollege\tHospital\tSpecial District", "no_homestead": false, "tax_rates": [{"entity": "DALLAS COUNTY\tDALLAS COLLEGE\tPARKLAND HOSPITAL\tUNASSIGNED\nHOMESTEAD EXEMPTION", "estimated_tax": 4561.0}], "current_tax_balance": 0.0, "current_levy": 5303.18, "prior_year_due": 0.0, "payment_history": [{"date": "2026-02-10", "amount": 5674.39, "tax_year": "2025", "payer": "TRULY TITLE INC"}, {"date": "2025-01-24", "amount": 5148.36, "tax_year": "2024", "payer": "LESLIE J DAVIDSION"}, {"date": "2024-02-01", "amount": 5004.01, "tax_year": "2023", "payer": "LAURA DAVIDSON"}, {"date": "2023-07-12", "amo