INSERT INTO cases VALUES(130,'TX-24-00067','101st District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2024-01-18','CLOSED','TAX DELINQUENCY','MOORE, CONNIE','[{"name": "CONNIE MOORE", "address": "920 KORY DR, MESQUITE, TX 75149", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "CONSTABLE PCT 2 / ATTORNEY", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Two citation attempts both returned unexecuted; dismissed before service achieved"}]','4421 BRIGHTWOOD DRIVE, GARLAND, TX',NULL,'26142800010050000','Perdue Brandon Fielder Collins & Mott','REECE, LINDA D.',7377.8000000000005798,2022,'[2022]',1,0,0,'[]',0,0,0,'Both citation attempts (Constable PCT 2 and attorney/mail) returned unexecuted; defendant never served before dismissal','medium',NULL,'2024-07-01','NON-SUIT/DISMISSAL BY PLAINTIFF / PETITIONER',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "GARLAND INDEPENDENT SCHOOL DISTRICT", "taxAmt": 2931.25, "penaltyInterest": 1430.45, "total": 4361.7}, {"entity": "CITY OF GARLAND", "taxAmt": 1791.73, "penaltyInterest": 874.37, "total": 2666.1}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC Peak Development | Senior Analyst Desk**\n**Case:** TX-24-00067 | **Property:** 4421 Brightwood Drive, Garland, TX 75040\n**Owner:** Connie Moore / Connie Blanchard | **Date:** 2025\n**Classification:** POST-DISMISSAL MONITOR | **Priority:** LOW-MODERATE\n\n---\n\n## ¶1 — PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe subject property is a 2002-built single-family residence in Duck Creek Estates Addition, Garland, sitting on Lot 5, Block 1 per Instrument 201100099546 of the Dallas County Deed Records. At 1,493 square feet with 24 years of age and a confirmed 30% depreciation flag in DCAD data, this is unambiguously a **structure play with deferred maintenance risk**, not a land play — the improvement carries the value here, not the dirt. DCAD pegs market value at **$301,260**, which for a 1,493 sqft 2002 structure in this Garland submarket implies a per-square-foot value of approximately **$201.78/sqft**, reasonable for Duck Creek Estates but potentially inflated relative to actual condition given the depreciation signal and absence of any cosmetic update evidence in the record. The 30% depreciation on a 24-year-old structure is not simply age-curve math — it indicates above-average physical wear, likely deferred maintenance across roof, HVAC, and interior finishes, which are the three cost centers that will dominate any rehab underwrite. The exterior material field returned blank in DCAD, which typically signals either a data gap or an unremarkable vinyl/brick-veneer composition that assessors often skip — not a red flag on its own, but worth a windshield inspection. The deed transfer date of **April 19, 2011** places Blanchard''s acquisition during the post-crash buyer''s market, suggesting she paid below current value and has substantial embedded equity. The ownership record shows **BLANCHARD CONNIE at 100%**, while the lawsuit names **CONNIE MOORE** — this is a maiden name / married name discrepancy, not a separate party, and both names resolve to the same individual. The **absence of a homestead exemption** is the single most operationally significant data point on the property side: it confirms this property is either rented, vacant, or otherwise not Connie''s primary residence as of the filing period. Her listed defendant address — **920 Kory Dr, Mesquite, TX 75149** — is where she actually','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-10T15:22:11.537672','2026-07-10T15:22:11.537672','2026-07-10T15:22:11.537672',1,'individual','high','LOT 5, BLOCK 1, DUCK CREEK ESTATES ADDITION, AKA 4421 BRIGHTWOOD DRIVE, CITY OF GARLAND, TEXAS AS RECORDED IN INSTRUMENT 201100099546 OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS','{"account_number": "26142800010050000", "market_value": 301260, "land_value": 65000, "improvement_value": 236260, "estimated_annual_taxes": 7214.34, "year_built": 2002, "effective_year_built": 2002, "actual_age": 24, "building_class": "16", "construction_type